agraph': 'Sometimes the gender gap has been yuge and sometimes more modestly endowed, but for months now men have remained pretty much for Donald J. Trump and women for Hillary Clinton. Last week’s debate, when Mrs. Clinton got a chance to bring up her opponent’s habit of calling women pigs, slobs and dogs, did nothing to narrow that divide.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Monster Sorority of Women Voters', 'kicker': 'News Analysis', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Our Monster Sorority', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Mary Jo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-01T19:58:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Mary Jo Murphy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Mary', 'middlename': 'Jo', 'lastname': 'Murphy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/47768bed-0447-5993-aebd-89b2bf4e9e45', 'word_count': 1228, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47768bed-0447-5993-aebd-89b2bf4e9e45'}, {'abstract': 'Readers responded to the deaths of the Miami Marlins pitcher and the golf champion Arnold Palmer.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/02/sports/letters-to-the-editor.html', 'snippet': 'Readers responded to the deaths of the Miami Marlins pitcher and t