ilsons-talk/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: Demonstrators disturb Prime Minister Harold Wilson at a church service in Brighton in October 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BRIGHTON — Prime Minister Harold Wilson was shouted down by demonstrators and scuffles broke out in a church here today [Oct. 2] as he mounted the pulpit to read the lesson. White-helmeted policemen stationed outside were called to break up the demonstration in the packed Dorset Gardens Methodist Church. Hymn books went flying and members of the congregation were crushed against the pews as the officers struggled in the aisles to drag the demonstrators out. They were mostly young men and girls and were led out shouting ‘‘you hypocrite’’ and ‘‘murderer’’ at the prime minster. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 449, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/blogs/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown/03oldiht-1966-wilsonbrown-superJu