 in October 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NIGERIA — An emergency airlift was organized in Nigeria today [Oct. 3] to rescue hunted Ibo tribesmen from widespread tribal violence in the Northern Region. More than 1,000 Ibos from the neighbouring Eastern Region have been killed in week-long rioting throughout the north, and the final death toll may climb above 2,000. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Ibos Saved From Massacre', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-03T14:16:57+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d9317c13-1d26-5226-bdac-f7ce324c779b', 'word_count': 103, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d9317c13-1d26-5226-bdac-f7ce324c779b'}, {'abstract': 'Daniel Bergner’s “Sing for Your Life” tells the incredible true story of Ryan Speedo Green’s unlikely rise to stardom.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/books/review/daniel-bergner-sing-for-your-life-ryan-speedo-green.html', 'snippet': 'Daniel Bergner’s “Sing for Your Life” tells the incredible true story of Ryan Speedo Green’s unlikely rise to stardom.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SING FOR YOUR LIFEA Story of Race, Music, and FamilyBy Daniel Bergner311 pp. A Lee Boudreaux Book/Little, Brown & Company. $28.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'cre