 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/adac6bd4-5b2c-5674-be2e-950205920254', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/adac6bd4-5b2c-5674-be2e-950205920254'}, {'abstract': 'A new show of the artist’s work includes candid etchings she made in the four years before her death — and portraits by Alex Van Gelder, from the same period.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/louise-bourgeois-turning-inwards.html', 'snippet': 'A new show of the artist’s work includes candid etchings she made in the four years before her death — and portraits by Alex Van Gelder, from the same period.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Somerset, in the west of England, is old farming country: a gently rolling, leafy landscape dotted with livestock. Here, in a suite of renovated agricultural buildings, Hauser & Wirth has its two-year-old out-of-town gallery, coupled with a working farm and a bustling art-lined restaurant serving local produce. With a salt-walled meat locker on public display and a loamy, autumnal smell floating in from surrounding pastures, the space has an earthy sensibility that might have appealed to Louise Bourgeois. The French-born, New York-based artist was noted for her forthright treatment of issues of the body and the mind; and in a series of little-known etchings now on view at the gallery-cum-country estate, she fuses the human body with botanical elements.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 826, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 826}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 744, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/art/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO/03tmag-bourgeois-slide-MLFO-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1487, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In the English Countryside, Intimate Works by — and of — Louise Bourgeois', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art Matters; Going Like 90', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hauser & Wirth', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bourgeois, Louise', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-03T21:04:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hettie Judah', 'person': [{'firstname':