atergoers, there’s no need to pack scuba gear or even a snorkel mask to plunge into the ocean deep. In Craig Francis and Rick Miller’s “Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea,” a frisky adaptation of the Jules Verne sci-fi saga at the New Victory Theater, a few actors, a few more props and some extremely nifty projections send the audience right to the seafloor. Hey, look out for that squid!', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 396, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 396}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 675, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04TWENTYLEAGUES/04TWENTYLEAGUES-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1350, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea,’ With a Message on the Environment', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Deep Dive for Kids, With a Bubbling Message', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea (Play)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Kidoons Network', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'WYRD Productions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Verne, Jules', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Miller, Rick (Theater Director)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Victory Theater', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-03T21:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexis Soloski', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexis', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Soloski', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b34a56fd-fb36-586d-b9b1-f940fda6db0b', 'word_count': 344, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b34a56fd-fb36-586d-b9b1-f940fda6db0b'}, {'abstract': 'With a long line of powerful women there, the heart of the French house, writes Alexander Fury, has always been female.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/03/t-magazine/fashion/maria-grazia-chiuri-dior-women-history-paris-fashion-week.html', 'snippet': 'With a long line of powerful women there, the heart of the French house, writes Alexander Fury, has always been female.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gabrielle “Coco” Chanel never did things by halves. When asked her opinion on Christian Dior’s “New Look” — the shorthand for the wasp-waisted, full-skirted silhouette Dior introduced to furor, acclaim and near universal adoption in his debut collection of 1947 — she snapped: “Look how ridiculous these women are, wearing clothes by a man who doesn’t know women, never had one, and dreams of being one.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/03tmag-diorpromo/03tmag-diorpromo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Maria Grazia Chiuri and the History of Women at Dior', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Christian Dior SA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chiuri, Maria Grazia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dior, Christian', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Paris Fashion Week', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-03T21:33:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Fury', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fury', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b1aec0bc-c937-5376-8889-f0c92e4cb584', 'word_count': 841, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b1aec0bc-c937-5376-8889-f0c92e4cb584'}, {'abstract': 'Ben Macintyre tells the story of mavericks who formed a commando unit that would become the model for special forces around the world.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/books/review-rogue-heroes-ben-macintyre.html', 'snippet': 'Ben Macintyre tells the story of mavericks who formed a commando unit that would become the model for special forces around the world.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ben Macintyre’s suspenseful new book, “Rogue Heroes,” about the founding of Britain’s S.A.S. during World War II, reads like a mashup of “The Dirty Dozen” and “The Great Escape,” with a sprinkling of “Ocean’s 11” thrown in for good measure. Like earlier Macintyre books set during that war (“Double Cross: The True Story of the D-Day Spies” and “Operation Mincemeat: How a Dead Man and a Bizarre Plan Fooled the Nazis and Assured an Allied Victory”), this volume features an ensemble of eccentrics, mavericks and malcontents. And, in this case, one visionary, David Stirling, who invented an elite commando unit that would become the prototype for a new kind of modern warfare, and the model for special forces around the world, including the Navy SEALs and the Army’s Delta Force.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 872, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 872}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 705, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/arts/04BOOKMACINTYRE/04BOOKMACINTYRE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1385, 'width': 953, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Rogue Heroes,’ the Birth of Britain’s Elite Special Forces', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '  Commandos Who Waged Elite War  ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': "Rogue Heroes: The History of the SAS, Britain's Secret Special Forces Unit That Sabotaged the Nazis and Changed the Nature of War (Book)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Macintyre, Ben', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-03T21:41:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/95fce254-bf5f-5704-b04e-ed720f50effe', 'word_count': 848, 'uri': 'nyt://article/95fce254-bf5f-5704-b04e-ed720f50effe'}, {'abstract': 'Whether they’re America’s house band or a living spectrum of soul to hip-hop, Roots rocks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/arts/music/roots-picnic-new-york-review.html', 'snippet': 'Whether they’re America’s house band or a living spectrum of soul to hip-hop, Roots rocks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a certain stripe of older fan, the Roots are exceptionalists who embody all of hip-hop’s potential as an extension of the soul music tradition, and who keep hip-hop viable as live performance. For a newer generation of fans, who come to them via their gig on Jimmy Fallon’s late-night show, they are America’s house band, polymaths who collaborate with stars on quirky viral videos and offer up musical cheers, jeers or arched eyebrows as the circumstance dictates.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page'