oard', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/57229cd5-17b4-5b7a-9d8c-de09c016fcc2', 'word_count': 583, 'uri': 'nyt://article/57229cd5-17b4-5b7a-9d8c-de09c016fcc2'}, {'abstract': 'Writers and critics from many quarters responded quickly to an Italian journalist’s excavation of financial records in an effort to identify the author who writes as Elena Ferrante.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/05/books/who-is-elena-ferrante-supporters-say-noyb.html', 'snippet': 'Writers and critics from many quarters responded quickly to an Italian journalist’s excavation of financial records in an effort to identify the author who writes as Elena Ferrante.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The readers of Elena Ferrante are devoted — and fiercely protective — of that anonymous Italian author. That much was clear from the swift and unforgiving backlash after an investigative journalist used financial documents to suggest in an article  published on Sunday that Anita Raja, an Italian translator, was behind Ms. Ferrante’s books.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/arts/03FERRANTE/03FERRANTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/03/arts/03FERRANTE/03FERRANTE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/arts/03FERRANTE/03FERRANTE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/arts/03FERRANTE/03FERRANTE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'su