-party-voters-know-what-they-want.html', 'snippet': 'And they don’t want to be told they will bear responsibility for President Trump. That would be the fault of the two-party system they despise.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Tuesday night, two men who want to be vice president will face off in a debate. If Bill Weld had his way, he’d be up on that stage, too.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04rollerWeb/04rollerWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Third-Party Voters Know What They Want', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Third-Party Voters Can Speak for Themselves', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third-Party Politics (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Gary E', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stein, Jill', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emma Roller', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emma', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roller', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b70725f9-587c-5480-986e-586233a3fb3b', 'word_count': 1828, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b70725f9-587c-5480-986e-586233a3fb3b'}, {'abstract': 'For Tim Kaine and Mike Pence, nothing can be said to be certain, except debate and taxes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/opinion/campaign-stops/speak-up-mr-vice-presidential-candidate-we-can-barely-hear-you.html', 'snippet': 'For Tim Kaine and Mike Pence, nothing can be said to be certain, except debate and taxes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Gail Collins: Arthur, we are on the cusp of another great moment in the campaign — vice-presidential debate! Tim Kaine takes on Mike Pence! Never has there been such an encounter since Sylvester Stallone took on Mr. T in Rocky III.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04conversationSub/04tue3web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Speak Up, Mr. Vice Presidential Candidate. We Can Barely Hear You.', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaine, Timothy M', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T07:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur C. Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6a9de6bd-7124-53b0-971e-c6a98de9d9ca', 'word_count': 1999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6a9de6bd-7124-53b0-971e-c6a98de9d9ca'}, {'abstract': 'Microfinance and small rooftop panels can transform lives in a country where the electric grid reaches just 25 percent of the population.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/opinion/in-rural-bangladesh-solar-power-dents-poverty.html', 'snippet': 'Microfinance and small rooftop panels can transform lives in a country where the electric grid reaches just 25 percent of the population.', 'lead_paragraph': 'KAKHIN BIMILE, Bangladesh — Kismat Ali is a 33-year-old mason living in Kakhin Bimile, a village a few hours drive from Dhaka, Bangladesh’s crowded capital. He lives in a large brick home on a dirt road with his wife, son, parents and five brothers. This semirural area is off the main electrical grid, so residents rely on kerosene lamps and electricity from wires strung across the village to a noisy privately owned diesel generator. It runs about five hours each night.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04fixes2/04fixes2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Rural Bangladesh, Solar Power Dents Poverty', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Solar Energy', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Rural Areas', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric Light and Power', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Microfinance', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poverty', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Bank', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Bangladesh', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'India', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T07:21:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amy Yee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/29d41ead-725b-561b-8cc7-f8dc270cb787', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/29d41ead-725b-561b-8cc7-f8dc270cb787'}, {'abstract': 'Across the country, spotty records and lax laws shield the financial interests of public officials, from presidential candidates on down.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/opinion/why-its-so-hard-to-see-politicians-financial-data.html', 'snippet': 'Across the country, spotty records and lax laws shield the financial interests of public officials, from presidential candidates on down.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You don’t learn much from tax returns,” Donald J. Trump said last week in the first presidential debate. That line may become as famous a gaffe as Gerald Ford’s claiming in a 1976 debate that Eastern Europe wasn’t under Soviet domination.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/opinion/04wihbey/04wihbey-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1369, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why It’s So Hard to See Politicians’ Financial Data', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Financial Disclosure, Wrapped in Secrecy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beaudet, Mike', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wihbey, John', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Taxes (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics and Official Misconduct', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'States (US)', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Corruption (Institutional)', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T07:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Wihbey and Mike Beaudet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wihbey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Beaudet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/230a07d9-9158-5c23-86dd-1519b9729e8f', 'word_count': 968, 'uri': 'nyt://article/230a07d9-9158-5c23-86dd-1519b9729e8f'}, {'abstract': 'O.K., it won’t rival the Trump-Clinton rumble for excitement, but the vice-presidential debate could be an important comparison of policy visions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/opinion/gov-pence-and-senator-kaine-face-off-in-farmville.html', 'snippet': 'O.K., it won’t rival the Trump-Clinton rumble for excitement, but the vice-presidential debate could be an important comparison of policy visions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s safe to say Tuesday’s vice-presidential debate won’t rival the Hillary Clinton-Donald Trump rumble for great television moments. It features two middle-aged, white, Midwest-raised politicians who call themselves “boring” (Tim Kaine) and “B-list” (Mike Pence). And running mates play an even smaller role than usual in 2016, given the outsized personalities at the top of the tickets. But if these two men are willing to seriously engage the issues (and the rest of us are willing to stay awake), they could provide useful insights into their sharply contrasting plans for the future.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 710, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/opinion/04tue3Web/04tue3Web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1419, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Senator Kaine and Gov. Pence: Face-Off in Farmville!', 'kicker': 'Editorial Observer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gov. Pence and Senator Kaine Face Off', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Williamson, Elizabeth', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaine, Timothy M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorial Observer', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T07:21:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Elizabeth Williamson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Elizabeth', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williamson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/7f5deb82-2b7d-5f75-9b69-5f853216ee3c', 'word_count': 540, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7f5deb82-2b7d-5f75-9b69-5f853216ee3c'}, {'abstract': 'The halting pace of the camera effort is striking for an agency that has pledged to make itself a model of technology-driven policing.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/04/nyregion/despite-national-trend-new-york-police-are-slow-to-adopt-body-cameras.html', 'snippet': 'The halting pace of the camera effort is striking for an agency that has pledged to make itself a model of technology-driven policing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The New York Police Department once seemed poised to be an early adopter of body cameras. A federal judge thought the technology could curb unwarranted stops and searches of black and Hispanic men. So in 2013, after finding the department’s stop-and-frisk practices unconstitutional, the judge ordered that a pilot program be established in at least five precincts.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/04/nyregion/04BODYCAMScombo/04BODYCAMScombo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/04/nyregion/04BODYCAMScombo/04BODYCAMScombo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201