 {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T09:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'Interview by Ana Marie Cox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Interview', 'middlename': 'Ana', 'lastname': 'Marie', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b5cd7ff-04fe-55dd-a766-d038adaa8524', 'word_count': 685, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b5cd7ff-04fe-55dd-a766-d038adaa8524'}, {'abstract': 'The theft of two 16th-century books from a Manhattan shop illustrates how the close-knit world of antiquarian booksellers keeps its treasures safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/05/nyregion/we-are-a-big-family-dealers-unite-against-thefts-of-rare-books.html', 'snippet': 'The theft of two 16th-century books from a Manhattan shop illustrates how the close-knit world of antiquarian booksellers keeps its treasures safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In Nantucket-red trousers and loafers, the customer looked the part of an upscale antiquarian book collector as he browsed 16th-century Italian texts on display in a chandelier-decked showroom inside a landmark brownstone on the Upper East Side of Manhattan. But it was a conspicuous outfit for a thief — moments after the man entered on that day last spring, cameras caught him stuffing two texts worth a total of more than $20,000, according to a bookseller, into an elegant case.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/17/nyregion/00BOOKS1/00BOOKS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thum