everyday life in Iraq in 2002 in the first half of his two-part film, “Homeland: Iraq Year Zero,” opening on Thursday. Shooting on video in his brother’s home near Baghdad, he shows his niece and nephews watching television one morning; a piece of state propaganda referring to Hussein as “Beloved Leader” soon gives way to a Looney Tune cartoon featuring Foghorn Leghorn.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 292, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 292}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 1009, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 1009, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/arts/05HOMELAND/05HOMELAND-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Homeland: Iraq Year Zero’ Chronicles a War-Torn Family', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Home Movie, So to Speak, With War as the Soundtrack', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Iraq War (2003-11)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Baghdad (Iraq)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Fahdel, Abbas', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-04T20:58:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/d63df527-df17-5e51-9fa1-2080ce73aeef', 'word_count': 548, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d63df527-df17-5e51-9fa1-2080ce73aeef'}, {'abstract': 'A new crop of home design books offer inspiration and escapism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/06/style/fall-design-books-to-inspire-home-decorating.html', 'snippet': 'A new crop of home design books offer inspiration and escapism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As temperatures drop and Canada geese catch thermals, one’s thoughts turn to redecorating for the indoor months ahead. This fall’s crop of home design books offers the usual inspiration and escapism.', 'print_section': 'F', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/style/06BOOKS1/06BOOKS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/09/28/style/06BOOKS1/06BOOKS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 6