RMVILLE, Va. — Senator Tim Kaine and Gov. Mike Pence repeatedly threw each other on the defensive over their running mates’ policies and character at the vice-presidential debate on Tuesday night, with Mr. Pence making little effort to directly rebut the near-constant attacks on Donald J. Trump’s fitness for the presidency.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Tim Kaine and Mike Pence Clash Sharply Over Their Running Mates', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Kaine and Pence  Clash on Merits of Their Tickets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martin, Jonathan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaine, Timothy M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-05T02:45:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Martin and Patrick Healy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Martin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Patrick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Healy', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c9ce7c5-89f4-54c3-b020-7ce91f008107', 'word_count': 1599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c9