heir only debate of the 2016 campaign, moderated by Elaine Quijano of CBS. Our chief television critic, James Poniewozik, and our media columnist, Jim Rutenberg, caught up with each other on Wednesday morning to discuss how the bottom-of-the-ticket debate played onscreen.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/us/06vpconvo/06vpconvo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Vice-Presidential Debate: How Do You Fact-Check a Headshake?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vice Presidents and Vice Presidency (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pence, Mike', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaine, Timothy M', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'CBS Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Quijano, Elaine (1975- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-05T13:27:35+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik and Jim Rutenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rutenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/90bc8b52-5d60-5c50-970f-f4be92cb52eb', 'word_count': 1691, 'uri': 'nyt://article/90bc8b52-5d60-5c50-970f-f4be92cb52eb'}, {'abstract': 'The Luxembourg & Dayan gallery is putting paintings and sculptures on view from this American artist, who died in 2007.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/arts/design/art-by-salvatore-scarpitta-from-vivid-paintings-to-fast-cars.html', 'snippet': 'The Luxembourg & Dayan gallery is putting paintings and sculptures on view from this American artist, who died in 2007.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The American painter and sculptor Salvatore Scarpitta has always seemed like the lost man in the lineup of durably famous artists — Robert Rauschenberg, Jasper Johns, Cy Twombly, Frank Stella — championed by the legendary dealer Leo Castelli. Scarpitta, who was raised in Los Angeles and died in 2007, never quite took off as a postwar pioneer. But then again, he never pursued anything resembling a standard art career: He was an unconventional painter who became an untrained car manufacturer. Opening Oct. 14 at the Luxembourg & Dayan gallery, “Salvatore Scarpitta 1956-1964” will trace his evolution, from his traumatized-looking paintings made with bandages and bulges to a turn in his sculpture toward the mid-1960s in which his automotive fascinations began to spawn racecars, a few of which actually worked (and were actually raced). (Through Dec. 23; 212-452-4646, luxembourgdayan.com.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD2/109WEEKAHEAD2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 730, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD2/109WEEKAHEAD2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 730}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD2/109WEEKAHEAD2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 842, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD2/109WEEKAHEAD2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1684, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD2/109WEEKAHEAD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD2/109WEEKAHEAD2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnail