 starts important conversations about injustice, but some aboriginal people say it plays down their continuing plight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/06/world/americas/winnipeg-canadian-museum-for-human-rights.html', 'snippet': 'Backers of the Canadian Museum for Human Rights say it starts important conversations about injustice, but some aboriginal people say it plays down their continuing plight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WINNIPEG, Manitoba — The Canadian Museum for Human Rights offers many opportunities for contemplation. A glass display case holds the bloodstained salwar kameez worn by Malala Yousafzai, the activist for girls’ education in Pakistan, during an assassination attempt by the Taliban. Video testimonials from survivors of the genocides in Rwanda, Ukraine and Bosnia aim to teach tolerance.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/06/world/06CANMUSEUM-web1/06CANMUSEUM-web1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Museum About Rights, and a Legacy of Uncomfortable Canadian Truths', 'kicker': 'Winnipeg Journal', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Museum About Rights, and an Uncomfortable Legacy', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Canadian Museum for Human Rights', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Canada', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Indigenous People', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Winnipeg (Manitoba)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-05T13:30:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Dan Levin', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Levin', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8a3b447b-00f7-5bfc-af40-5c3898e4e9be', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8a3b447b-00f7-5bfc-af40-5c3898e4e9be'}, {'abstract': 'But don’t expect Carrie Bradshaw in the suburbs. This time, Ms. Parker plays a woman navigating a failing marriage.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/arts/television/sarah-jessica-parker-returns-to-hbo-with-divorce.html', 'snippet': 'But don’t expect Carrie Bradshaw in the suburbs. This time, Ms. Parker plays a woman navigating a failing marriage.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twelve years after the women of “Sex and the City” swilled their last cosmos, Sarah Jessica Parker is returning to HBO with a new series — one that might suggest her alter ego’s long-awaited “I love you” didn’t work out quite as planned. But don’t expect Carrie Bradshaw in the ’burbs. In “Divorce,” debuting at 10 p.m. on Sunday, Oct. 9, Ms. Parker plays Frances, an arty type turned corporate recruiter navigating marital purgatory in Westchester County with her husband, Robert (Thomas Haden Church), a flailing real-estate developer, and their two children. But when a friend’s 50th-birthday party turns amusingly violent, life’s niggling disappointments explode into vivid relief, and some serious navel-gazing ensues. The show’s title pretty much sums it up as Frances and Robert deal with each other’s infidelities — hers physical, his emotional — and the flatlining of their union, and conclude that they’re better off apart. If only they could make a clean break. The discourse, achingly knowing and bracingly comical, will ring familiar to fans of Amazon’s “Catastrophe” and its gloriously sniping Sharon Horgan, this series’s creator.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 289, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 289}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 493, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD8/109WEEKAHEAD8-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 985, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sarah Jessica Parker Returns to HBO With ‘Divorce’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Television; There’s Trouble in the Suburbs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Parker, Sarah Jessica', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Church, Thomas Haden', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Home Box Office', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Horgan, Sharon (1970- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Divorce (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-05T13:32:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kathryn Shattuck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kathryn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Shattuck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/51b0b76f-4b68-594c-a3b7-a4ab0e320a6e', 'word_count': 181, 'uri': 'nyt://article/51b0b76f-4b68-594c-a3b7-a4ab0e320a6e'}, {'abstract': 'Tim Rushton’s “Black Diamond,” a two-act work with science-fiction touches, will be performed at the Joyce Theater several times.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/arts/dance/danish-dance-theater-at-the-joyce-with-a-sci-fi-look.html', 'snippet': 'Tim Rushton’s “Black Diamond,” a two-act work with science-fiction touches, will be performed at the Joyce Theater several times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tim Rushton’s “Black Diamond” begins with an explosion, filling the stage with silver confetti and the members of Danish Dance Theater — some masked and resembling science-fiction aliens, others wrapped in (and seeking to extricate themselves from) enveloping fabric. As the two-act piece proceeds, audiences may wonder if that big bang is one of apocalyptic destruction. Maybe. But maybe not. The human spirit may ultimately triumph, as dancers aspire toward a shining ball of light: the light of truth, perhaps?', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD1/109WEEKAHEAD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 312, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD1/109WEEKAHEAD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 312}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD1/109WEEKAHEAD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 532, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD1/109WEEKAHEAD1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1064, 'width': 2048, 'su