Tidal has staked its reputation on access to A-list acts, a muscle it is flexing again for its second annual charity concert on Saturday, Oct. 15, at Barclays Center. (Proceeds from ticket sales benefit education nonprofits.) Returning from last year’s event, which raised $1.5 million, are Beyoncé, Nicki Minaj and T.I.; Alicia Keys and Lauryn Hill are also to perform. A more eclectic bunch of Tidal allies — the Latin pop singer Prince Royce, the singsong rapper Lil Yachty, the political indie-pop project Blood Orange — also fit under this big tent of artist activism, and may have more to prove. (tidal.com/us/1015.)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD7/109WEEKAHEAD7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD7/109WEEKAHEAD7-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD7/109WEEKAHEAD7-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD7/109WEEKAHEAD7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 601, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD7/109WEEKAHEAD7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 601}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/arts/109WEEKAHEAD7/109WEEKAHEAD7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1023, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype':