: 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/09/28/opinion/28johnsonWeb/28johnsonWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Election Engagement', 'kicker': 'Picture Prompts', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-06T08:35:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a583985-2210-5f78-8b66-a4eb605592e3', 'word_count': 91, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a583985-2210-5f78-8b66-a4eb605592e3'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether adultery can be a moral choice and on starting to smoke after you sign up for insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/magazine/is-it-ok-to-find-sexual-satisfaction-outside-your-marriage.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on whether adultery can be a moral choice and on starting to smoke after you sign up for insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am married and have three children with my husband. For the most part, our lives are happy. My husband and I have a good relationship and are active in our children’s lives. However, I am utterly unsatisfied sexually. I need a bit more than occasional vanilla sex to feel content in that area (nothing too crazy, mind you). When my husband and I first started dating some years ago, I gently brought this matter up to him a handful of times during the course of regular conversation. His answers to me seemed to imply that he was the type who took some time to warm up to new ideas. With this in mind, I moved forward with him, believing that eventually our sex life would become more adventurous. It hasn’t. It has been seven years since we became a committed couple, and if anything, our sex has become more boring and certainly less frequent. ', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/magazine/09ethicist/09ethicist-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 403, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/magazine/09ethicist/09ethicist-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 617, 'width': 403, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/magazine/09ethicist/09ethicist-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/magazine/09ethicist/09ethicist-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/magazine/09ethicist/09ethicist-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Is It O.K. to Find Sexual Satisfaction Outside Your Marriage?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Is It O.K. to Have Another Man Satisfy Me Sexually, Since My Husband Can’t?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ADULTERY', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lying', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Life Insurance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-06T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kwame Anthony Appiah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kwame', 'middlename': 'Anthony', 'lastname': 'Appiah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3eb09cb1-ed0f-5fb3-8670-5587129170e9', 'word_count': 1485, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3eb09cb1-ed0f-5fb3-8670-5587129170e9'}, {'abstract': 'A generative spirit and symbolic power elevate an Islam scholar’s life and works.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-the-life-of-marshall-hodgson.html', 'snippet': 'A generative spirit and symbolic power elevate an Islam scholar’s life and works.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Viewed in the least charitable terms, academia is a small fraternity of ambitious backbiters engaged in the production of work so dense that only other members of the order can hope to understand it. But some scholars arrive on the scene bearing such a combination of intellect, urgency and charisma that their achievements resonate long after the Festschrift is printed and the memorial lecture empties out.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/magazine/09lor/09mag-09lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, '