nuclear weapons in the Vietnam War in October 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/06/1966-nuclear-weapons-and-vietnam/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The U.S. President Johnson avoids to comment on the potential use of nuclear weapons in the Vietnam War in October 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Johnson avoided direct comment today [Oct. 6] on potential use of nuclear weapons in Vietnam but said U.S. policy there is to “provide the maximum deterrence with a minimum involvement.” The statement came during a White House press conference when the president was asked for comment on a statement made on Monday by former President Dwight D. Eisenhower. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Nuclear Weapons and Vietnam', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Eisenhower, Dwight David', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Johnson, Lyndon Baines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'NUCLEAR WEAPONS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-06T14:19:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ca4b1cef-79ab-51d6-9eda-776b2392cdcc', 'word_count': 121, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ca4b1cef-79ab-51d6-9eda-776b2392cdcc'}, {'abstract': 'Both presidential candidates are increasingly staking their fortune