alleys-data.html', 'snippet': 'They also don’t want anyone to talk about it, a fact that has riled a number of tech companies that are chafing under gag orders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A gentle reminder: The Justice Department backing off demands that Apple help it break the security of an iPhone six months ago does not mean law enforcement isn’t still very interested in the information gathered and protected by tech companies.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Daily Report: The Feds Can’t Resist Silicon Valley’s Data', 'kicker': 'Bits', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computer Security', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Justice Department', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signal (Open Whisper Systems)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-06T16:05:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jim Kerstetter', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kerstetter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/88afe525-7ef8-5d8f-9539-9d7a9996bcd6', 'word_count': 288, 'uri': 'nyt://article/88afe525-7ef8-5d8f-9539-9d7a9996bcd6'}, {'abstract': 'Windows were smashed and cars were wrecked in the bombing, the latest in a string of terrorist attacks in Turkey.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/07/world/europe/istanbul-turkey-motorcycle-bomb.html', 'snippet': 'Windows were smashed and cars were wrecked in the bombing, the latest in a string o