-a-weapon-in-banks-regulatory-fight.html', 'snippet': 'Big lenders had hoped to piggyback on Wells Fargo’s small Wall Street presence to resist proposals to curb pay and ban merchant banking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Wells Fargo has deprived banks of a Washington standard-bearer. Big lenders hoped to piggyback on their rival’s lack of Wall Street taint to resist proposals to curb pay and ban merchant banking. But the fake-accounts scandal weakens Wells Fargo’s ability to lead the charge.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Wells Fargo Scandal Blunts a Weapon in Banks’ Regulatory Fight', 'kicker': 'Breakingviews', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JPMorgan Chase & Company', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Wells Fargo & Company', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Dimon, James', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stumpf, John G', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-06T17:21:17+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gina Chon', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chon', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fec1c79-9b22-585e-84e5-b685fa62c7ee', 'word_count': 360, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fec1c79-9b22-585e-84e5-b685fa62c7ee'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Trump has fomented divisions that began before he started his campaign, capitalizing on working-class whites’ anger at the party establishment.', 'web_url': 'https://ww