he owner of the eight-unit apartment building nine times to try to force repairs. And the landlord owes $20,000 in fines and more than $235,000 in unpaid interest and water, sewer and other bills.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1639, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/nyregion/07HOUSING/07HOUSING-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'New York City Sells Landlords’ Debts, but Buildings Fall Into Limbo, Critics Say', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'City Sells Landlords’ Debts, but Buildings Face Limbo', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Silver-Greenberg, Jessica', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Landlords', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Affordable Housing', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Buildings Department (NYC)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, Letitia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Stringer, Scott M', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-06T20:57:15+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jessica Silver-Greenberg and Kim Barker', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jessica', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Silver-Greenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kim', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barker', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/690d4804-66f8-5982-b220-cd0245dc7600', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/690d4804-66f8-5982-b220-cd0245dc7600'}, {'abstract': 'André Téchiné’s film centers on schoolyard combatants whose violent tussles begin to have an undertone of repressed desire.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/07/movies/review-in-being-17-2-boys-teeter-between-animosity-and-attraction.html', 'snippet': 'André Téchiné’s film centers on schoolyard combatants whose violent tussles begin to have an undertone of repressed desire.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To fight or to fall in love: That is the choice two antagonistic high school cl