ine': {'original': 'By ALEC COHEN', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alec', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'COHEN', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Video', '_id': 'nyt://video/235b477f-85b5-5cdb-b1ce-363114a2f9d6', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://video/235b477f-85b5-5cdb-b1ce-363114a2f9d6'}, {'abstract': 'A richly seasoned dish with cashews and coconut makes a satisfying vegetarian main course.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/12/dining/green-beans-recipe-video.html', 'snippet': 'A richly seasoned dish with cashews and coconut makes a satisfying vegetarian main course.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Just as soon as I had devoured the sautéed celery with mustard seeds and coconut that my friend Linta made for dinner one night, I immediately wanted to make a version of it at home.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Spicy Green Beans, at the Center of the Plate', 'kicker': 'A Good Appetite', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Spicy Green Beans Carry the Meal', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clark, Melissa', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Celery', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetarianism', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-07T16:17:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Melissa Clark', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Melissa', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Clark', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6513ad63-ea15-57a7-830e-9e3d82cac8d5', 'word_count': 445, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6513ad63-ea15-57a7-830e-9e3d82cac8d5'}, {'abstract': 'In “Weapons of Math Destruction,” No. 5 on the education best-seller list, Cathy O’Neil says our reliance on algorithms exacerbates whatever inequality already exists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/books/review/the-story-behind-this-weeks-best-sellers.html', 'snippet': 'In “Weapons of Math Destruction,” No. 5 on the education best-seller list, Cathy O’Neil says our reliance on algorithms exacerbates whatever inequality already exists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tyrant in the Machine: Cathy O’Neil had been working as a quant at a hedge fund for about a year when the global economy collapsed. In her introduction to “Weapons of Math Destruction,” No. 5 on the monthly education list and longlisted for the National Book Award, O’Neil — who holds a Ph.D. in mathematics from Harvard — recounts how the 2008 crash made her realize the enormous havoc that could be wreaked “by mathematicians wielding magic formulas.” The crisis showed that computer technology could combine with mathematics “to multiply the chaos and misfortune,” yet years later we continue to be enthralled by algorithms. We use them in teacher evaluations, hiring decisions, even sentencing rulings in the criminal justice system. We rely on Big Data more than ever before.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/books/review/07inside-list/07inside-list-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/07/books/review/07inside-list/07inside-list-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/books/review/07inside-list/07inside-list-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/books/review/07inside-list/07inside-list-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 261, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/07/books/review/07inside-list/07inside-list-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 266, 'width': 261, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Story Behind This Week’s Best Sellers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Inside the List', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-07T16:27:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Szalai', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Szalai', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'List', '_id': 'nyt://article/54af4f43-2831-5706-8726-ec8b69891309', 'word_count': 488, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54af4f43-2831-5706-8726-ec8b69891309'}, {'abstract': 'Sales have begun at 242 Broome, a 14-story condo that is part of the massive Essex Crossing redevelopment project on the Lower East Side.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/09/realestate/redefining-the-lower-east.html', 'snippet': 'Sales have begun at 242 Broome, a 14-story condo that is part of the massive Essex Crossing redevelopment project on the Lower East Side.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At the corner of Broome and Ludlow Streets, amid the tenement buildings of the Lower East Side, condominium sales began last month at a 14-story anodized aluminum and glass tower that will open in 2018. With a champagne hue to its facade, the building, 242 Broome, is just one piece of Essex Crossing, a $1 billion redevelopment project that will redefine the character of an area that lay fallow for nearly 50 years.', 'print_section': 'RE', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 821, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 821}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 749, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/realestate/09BROOME3/09BROOME3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1498, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Redefi