ch of the cuts planned by OPEC.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Little more than a week after the OPEC cartel moved to reduce oil supplies on the glutted global market, embattled Libya has reopened a major seaport terminal for oil exports and has announced that it intends to expand production through the rest of the year.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Libya Starts Expanding Oil Exports — for Now, at Least', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Libya Starts Expanding Oil Exports, Though Some Experts Doubt It Will Last', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Oil (Petroleum) and Gasoline', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Krauss, Clifford', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Libya', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Organization of the Petroleum Exporting Countries', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Oil Corp of Libya', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-07T22:22:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'Energy & Environment ', 'byline': {'original': 'By Clifford Krauss', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Clifford', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krauss', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5df2c825-5ef2-5dfe-a6eb-3b4849e6b4ca', 'word_count': 740, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5df2c825-5ef2-5dfe-a6eb-3b4849e6b4ca'}, {'abstract': 'The president might take in a Chicago Cubs playoff game while visiting his adopted home city for the weekend.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/08/us/politics/obama-votes-in-chicago-while-on-a-fun