(NYC)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-08T03:33:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rick Rojas and Alan Feuer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rick', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rojas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Alan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Feuer', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0d290d0-fe78-591d-8bb5-74eac6a9a532', 'word_count': 1033, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0d290d0-fe78-591d-8bb5-74eac6a9a532'}, {'abstract': 'Matthew came ashore in McClellanville, S.C., as a Category 1 storm. Officials in Georgia, North Carolina and Florida reported deaths tied to the storm.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/08/us/hurricane-matthew.html', 'snippet': 'Matthew came ashore in McClellanville, S.C., as a Category 1 storm. Officials in Georgia, North Carolina and Florida reported deaths tied to the storm.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hurricane Matthew made landfall Saturday morning near McClellanville, S.C., about 40 miles northeast of Charleston, as a Category 1 storm with sustained winds of 75 miles per hour. Georgia, South Carolina and North Carolina were lashed with torrential rains as the storm sideswiped those states on its path up the coast.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/08/us/politics/08MATTHEW-4/08MATTHEW-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/08/us/politics/08MATTHEW-4/08MATTHEW-4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/08/u