, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T05:17:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/883db726-7c3e-5ebb-b11e-8e0bd4b84147', 'word_count': 107, 'uri': 'nyt://article/883db726-7c3e-5ebb-b11e-8e0bd4b84147'}, {'abstract': 'While expectations for Mr. Trump were low, many commentators and critics thought that he allayed concerns among supporters that his candidacy was finished.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/us/politics/who-won-the-debate.html', 'snippet': 'While expectations for Mr. Trump were low, many commentators and critics thought that he allayed concerns among supporters that his candidacy was finished.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald J. Trump’s campaign appeared to be crumbling as he entered the second presidential debate against Hillary Clinton, with Republicans withdrawing support for his candidacy after the disclosure of a vulgar recording that showed him bragging about sexual assault. Facing a barrage of tough questions, the Republican nominee managed to scrape through, evading questions, fabricating answers and attacking his opponent in deeply personal terms.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/us/politics/doug-debate-stl-403/doug-debate-stl-403-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/09/us/politics/doug-debate-stl-403/doug-debate-stl-403-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/09/us/politics/doug-debate-stl-403/doug-debate-stl-403-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType'