middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Chen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2f950f7b-ad09-54c4-9502-e78afb167c12', 'word_count': 1816, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2f950f7b-ad09-54c4-9502-e78afb167c12'}, {'abstract': 'Many schools in the U.S. are off, so we’re taking a break ourselves — but should this holiday be known as “Columbus Day” or “indigenous Peoples Day”?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/10/learning/a-short-fall-break-but-what-should-we-call-it.html', 'snippet': 'Many schools in the U.S. are off, so we’re taking a break ourselves — but should this holiday be known as “Columbus Day” or “indigenous Peoples Day”?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Many schools in the United States are off for Columbus Day, so we’re taking a short break ourselves — but, as The Times reports, we may not be calling this early fall holiday “Columbus Day” for much longer:', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'A Short Fall Break, but What Should We Call It?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T07:50:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katherine Schulten', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katherine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schulten', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/30f1e9a5-f5ed-5c4a-9675-93acde57b28a', 'word_count': 315, 'uri': 'nyt://article/30f1e9a5-f5ed-5c4a-9675-93acde57b28a'}, {'abstract': 'Fred Lyons’s longtime muse is his hometown, San Francisco, whose streets and people have always beckoned him to dive in with camera in hand, day or night.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/10/san-francisco-noir-photos-from-40s-50s-fred-lyon/', 'snippet': 'Fred Lyons’s longtime muse is his hometown, San Francisco, whose streets and people have always beckoned him to dive in with camera in hand, day or night.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Fred Lyon is 92 years old and has photographed his hometown, San Francisco, for more than 70 years. His rich black-and-white scenes conjure a bygone era, when flash powder still existed, being alone with your thoughts was common, and the famed cable cars were public transportation for locals, rather than rolling tourist traps headed to Fisherman’s Wharf.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'San Francisco Noir: Photos From the ’40s and ’50s', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lyon, Fred (1924- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Leica Gallery', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'San Francisco (Calif)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T08:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Blaustein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Blaustein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eed61f2c-e50c-5759-809f-d75b09f5ae1f', 'word_count': 862, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eed61f2c-e50c-5759-809f-d75b09f5ae1f'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The U.S. Navy extends service limits to try to tackle a shortage of experienced officers in October 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/10/1966-older-officers-are-kept-on-the-job/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of the International Herald Tribune: The U.S. Navy extends service limits to try to tackle a shortage of experienced officers in October 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The navy, battling a serious shortage of experienced officers, now is permitting older officers twice passed over for promotion to stay on the job, sources revealed today [Oct. 9]. Such men normally are forced to leave active service. This was learned in the wake of the Navy’s announcement Friday that it will continue to extend the duties of an estimated 1,000 pilots and other highly skilled officers for another year to meet Vietnam needs. And, in Saigon, the U.S. military command announced that some selected officers in advisory and staff positions in the various services will serve up to two years, double the normal tour. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': '1966: Older Officers Are Kept on the Job', 'kicker': 'IHT Retrospective', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vietnam War', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ho Chi Minh City (Vietnam)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Vietnam', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T08:09:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'byline': {'original': 'By International Herald Tribune', 'person': [{'firstname': 'International', 'middlename': 'Herald', 'lastname': 'Tribune', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e7b3a5e-24de-59f7-be76-6cf8e0b73870', 'word_count': 226, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e7b3a5e-24de-59f7-be76-6cf8e0b73870'}, {'abstract': 'iO Tillett Wright’s debut memoir, “Darling Days,” is about growing up in the bohemian East Village of the 1980s and ’90s.', 'web_url': 'https://www