soning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Bacteria', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Food', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hygiene and Cleanliness', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'The Upshot', 'byline': {'original': 'By Aaron E. Carroll', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Aaron', 'middlename': 'E.', 'lastname': 'Carroll', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/37576b1a-dc30-511c-b6e7-84bc4d48c3d8', 'word_count': 953, 'uri': 'nyt://article/37576b1a-dc30-511c-b6e7-84bc4d48c3d8'}, {'abstract': 'Amenities like five times as many stalls for women, and monitors showing the vacant ones, aim to make sure traffic is the only delay to worry about.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/world/what-in-the-world/japan-toilet-award.html', 'snippet': 'Amenities like five times as many stalls for women, and monitors showing the vacant ones, aim to make sure traffic is the only delay to worry about.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The kids are hungry, the driver has a headache and everyone has to go to the bathroom. If you’re traveling by car on a holiday weekend, the last thing you want to find at a roadside rest stop is a long line for a toilet.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/05/world/what-in-the-world/wit_japan-bathrooms3/wit_japan-bathrooms3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/05/world/what-in-the-world/wit_japan-bathrooms3/wit_japan-bathrooms3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'sub