en making.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/world/americas/jeremie-haiti-hurricane-matthew.html', 'snippet': 'Along with hundreds of lives, the storm wiped out much of the progress that the isolated city, Jérémie, had been making.', 'lead_paragraph': 'JÉRÉMIE, Haiti — Things had been looking up in Jérémie, a coastal city marooned on the tip of Haiti’s southern peninsula. It had recently gotten its first decent road link to the rest of the country, a new highway through the rugged mountains that brought development. Cellphone service had finally begun, enabling farmers and businesses to flourish. The city was racing into the 21st century, dreaming of advanced agriculture and tourism in one of Haiti’s few nature preserves.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In Haiti, a City’s Race Into the 21st Century Is Ruined by a Hurricane', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Haitian City Was Finally Prospering. Then Came the Storm.', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ahmed, Azam', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Haiti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hurricanes and Tropical Storms', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T15:56:48+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Americas', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azam Ahmed', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ahmed', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/243a6db6-7014-583c-9c7f-23deac9ad24c', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/243a6db6-7014-583c-9c7f-23deac9ad24c'}, {'abstract': 'An extraordinary backstage confrontation between Mr. Trump’s campaign and the staff of the Presidential Co