er Café, on the East River, a goal is to provide a classic high-level breakfast “in the style of the grand hotels of Europe,” said the owner, Michael O’Keeffe. Though he is still tweaking the menu, his weekday eye-opener features choices like smoked salmon Benedict or avocado toast with poached eggs, and wines, Champagne and gentle pastel-hued cocktails. “Everyone stays for a long time, an hour and a half or two, relaxing away from the hustle of the city in a celebratory setting, ordering cocktails, Champagne and a surprising amount of caviar,” he said: Breakfast 8:30 to 11:30 a.m. Monday to Friday, the River Café, 1 Water Street (Old Fulton Street), Fulton Ferry, Brooklyn, 718-522-5200, rivercafe.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1/12BURNER-CAFE-WEB1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'t