 Rezoning', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Education (K-12)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Zoning', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Upper West Side (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-10T17:00:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Letters', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Letter', '_id': 'nyt://article/f697ad57-4590-5f69-b0d2-02bb76e9b23a', 'word_count': 220, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f697ad57-4590-5f69-b0d2-02bb76e9b23a'}, {'abstract': 'One diamond-rimmed roller coaster is a meditation on the passage of time.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/10/t-magazine/fashion/hermes-pearl-cuff.html', 'snippet': 'One diamond-rimmed roller coaster is a meditation on the passage of time.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The multifaceted Parisian designer Pierre Hardy says the bold jewelry he creates for the house of Hermès is inspired by shape and feeling rather than particular gemstones. This dizzyingly sinuous cuff, nearly three inches high, is a diamond-rimmed roller coaster of 150 pearls in varying sizes, as well as a meditation on the passage of time. Within the curvilinear rose-gold armature, the pearls seem to flow from day into night, shifting in shade from the luminous white of a snowy morning to the bottomless gray-black of midnight.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '86', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/hermes-cuff/hermes-cuff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/03/t-magazine/hermes-cuff/hermes-cuff-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', '