reen Chile Company sells New Mexico chiles jarred or fresh roasted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/12/dining/hatch-chiles-zia.html', 'snippet': 'Zia Green Chile Company sells New Mexico chiles jarred or fresh roasted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'New Mexico is known for its chiles from the Hatch Valley in the southern part of the state; chiles with varying heat levels are grown there and labeled Hatch. Zia Green Chile Company of Brooklyn sells jars of medium-hot or hot green chiles from Hatch, along with mild red; all are simply cooked, diced and preserved with lime, garlic and salt. The medium-hot green is vegetal and smoky, the hot is powerful, and the red has more fire than you would expect. They’re worth keeping in the refrigerator as a go-to condiment or spicy addition to recipes. The company also sells fresh roasted chiles from New Mexico; the 2016 harvest is ready for pre-order for shipping in coming weeks: Zia Green Chiles, 16-ounce jars, $10; roasted chiles, $35 for five pounds, www.ziagreenchileco.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/dining/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB/12BURNER-CHILE-WEB-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'wi