has had a bigger impact on men. In an NBC News/SurveyMonkey poll conducted before the release of the tape, 45 percent of likely male voters said Mr. Trump does not respect women. Post-tape, that share rose to 55 percent.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Male Voters Finally Get Trump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Men Finally Get Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Men and Boys', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Anna North', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Anna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'North', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/efdf7cb3-2d38-5c23-9698-1c42be6ae6c0', 'word_count': 246, 'uri': 'nyt://article/efdf7cb3-2d38-5c23-9698-1c42be6ae6c0'}, {'abstract': 'Across the globe, a slim chance of winning in a lottery can get people to vote, pay taxes, drive slower or make sex safe.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/opinion/for-better-citizenship-scratch-and-win.html', 'snippet': 'Across the globe, a slim chance of winning in a lottery can get people to vote, pay taxes, drive slower or make sex safe.', 'lead_paragraph': 'China, with its largely cash economy, has a huge problem with tax evasion. Not just grand tax evasion, but the everyday “no receipt, please” kind, even though there have been harsh penalties: Before 2011, some forms of tax evasion were even punishable by death.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'For Better Citizenship, Scratch and Win', 'kicker': 'Fixes', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Lotteries', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Traffic Accidents and Safety', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Times', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lesotho', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Los Angeles (Calif)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philadelphia (Pa)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T07:21:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tina Rosenberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tina', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rosenberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/1d435b6d-f018-566a-8e22-9499c625ed63', 'word_count': 1801, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1d435b6d-f018-566a-8e22-9499c625ed63'}, {'abstract': 'Brooks and Collins on the debate we could be having and the one we are actually having.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/opinion/campaign-stops/when-they-go-low-do-we-have-to-go-too.html', 'snippet': 'Brooks and Collins on the debate we could be having and the one we are actually having.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arthur Brooks: Hi, Gail. Well, the race has defied my expectations and hit a new moral low. Where to start — the insult-driven second debate, the sensational pre-debate press conference Trump held on Facebook with a jury of Bill Clinton’s accusers, the revelation that Mrs. Clinton told Wall Street bankers that one has to have “private” and “public” positions, or Trump’s videotaped Caligula impression from 2005 that has dominated the news since Friday? You choose.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 670, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1339, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11conversationWeb/11conversationWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'When They Go Low, Do We Have to Go, Too?', 'kicker': 'The Conversation', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T07:21:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Arthur C. Brooks and Gail Collins', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Arthur', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Gail', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Collins', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3a7fc4b4-66b4-5fa6-8bd1-c88dfb37588c', 'word_count': 1500, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3a7fc4b4-66b4-5fa6-8bd1-c88dfb37588c'}, {'abstract': 'The justices tell other judges to act in ways they themselves don’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/opinion/the-supreme-court-is-being-hypocritical.html', 'snippet': 'The justices tell other judges to act in ways they themselves don’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Supreme Court’s motto may be “equal justice under law.” But sometimes it seems more like “do as we say, not as we do.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11roth/11roth-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1151, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Supreme Court Is Being Hypocritical', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Supreme Court Is Being Hypocritical', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roth, Gabriel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conflicts of Interest', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T07:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gabe Roth', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gabe', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roth', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3799c73f-bd0b-542e-a09d-4090a3e1a518', 'word_count': 753, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3799c73f-bd0b-542e-a09d-4090a3e1a518'}, {'abstract': 'President Obama must cut off military aid to Saudi Arabia unless it ends the carnage and returns to peace talks.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/opinion/americas-moral-duty-in-yemen.html', 'snippet': 'President Obama must cut off military aid to Saudi Arabia unless it ends the carnage and returns to peace talks.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Airstrikes by a Saudi-led coalition that devastated a funeral in Yemen on Saturday make it clear that the United States must end its complicity in a civil war that has caused a humanitarian catastrophe in one of the world’s poorest countries and fueled extremism. It is within President Obama’s power to do so. Saudi Arabia and its Gulf state allies depend on Washington for aircraft, munitions, training and in-flight refueling. The United States also helps Saudi Arabia guard its borders.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 342, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 342}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 584, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11tue1/11tue1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1168, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Moral Duty in Yemen', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America’s Moral Duty in Yemen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Defense and Military Forces', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Yemen', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Saudi Arabia', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'War Crimes, Genocide and Crimes Against Humanity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kerry, John', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houthis', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Civilian Casualties', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T07:21:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/5001e888-1d05-50d6-b1b0-8b55e33c6337', 'word_count': 629, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5001e888-1d05-50d6-b1b0-8b55e33c6337'}, {'abstract': 'Politics is an effort to make human connection, but Trump seems incapable of that.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/opinion/donald-trumps-sad-lonely-life.html', 'snippet': 'Politics is an effort to make human connection, but Trump seems incapable of that.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The point of town hall debates is that regular voters get to ask questions. In every town hall I’ve seen, the candidate turns to the voter, listens attentively and directs the answer at least partially back to that person.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/11/opinion/11brooksWeb/11brooksWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'heigh