rint_headline': 'Black Lives Imagined', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gay, Roxane', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Picoult, Jodi', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Small Great Things (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roxane Gay', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roxane', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gay', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9e73bb40-2642-538b-bece-f2d9e816d241', 'word_count': 1249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9e73bb40-2642-538b-bece-f2d9e816d241'}, {'abstract': 'By kneeling during the national anthem, the 49ers quarterback has ignited a new era of activism by athletes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/magazine/how-colin-kaepernicks-protest-is-connecting-playing-fields-to-the-streets.html', 'snippet': 'By kneeling during the national anthem, the 49ers quarterback has ignited a new era of activism by athletes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A few days after the first presidential debate, LeBron James took a stand: He endorsed Hillary Clinton for president. The reasons he cited ranged from a belief that Clinton would “build on the legacy” of his “good friend” Barack Obama to her good works on behalf of children. James concluded with a passage about the “violence, of every kind, the African-American community is experiencing in our streets and seeing on our TVs.” He went on to say we need to be “unified” and “stand together — no matter where we are from or the color of our skin.” The measured tone was an echo of his appearance at the ESPY Awards in July, where he and his fellow N.B.A. stars Dwyane Wade, Carmelo Anthony and Chris Paul spoke out in a joint speech for “uniting communities” and ending violence.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 429, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 429}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 732, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/magazine/12onsports2/12onsports2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1310, 'width': 1832, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Colin Kaepernick’s Protest Is Connecting Playing Fields to the Streets', 'kicker': 'On Sports', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How Colin Kaepernick’s Protest Is Connecting Playing Fields to the Streets', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kang, Jay Caspian', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kaepernick, Colin', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'James, LeBron', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Police Brutality, Misconduct and Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests and Riots', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Blacks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Black People', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Athletics and Sports', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jay Caspian Kang', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jay', 'middlename': 'Caspian', 'lastname': 'Kang', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a831dfb-52d2-5ad4-905f-9d0f3ee01fb1', 'word_count': 1520, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a831dfb-52d2-5ad4-905f-9d0f3ee01fb1'}, {'abstract': 'When a 70-year-old campaigns for the White House, it’s no surprise that questions of strength and vigor might be raised. And when his opponent is a woman, it’s no surprise that she’s the one accused of lacking it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/magazine/whats-really-behind-trumps-obsession-with-clintons-stamina.html', 'snippet': 'When a 70-year-old campaigns for the White House, it’s no surprise that questions of strength and vigor might be raised. And when his opponent is a woman, it’s no surprise that she’s the one accused of lacking it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To Donald Trump, everything is negotiable, even getting old. At 70 — about 16 months older than Hillary Clinton — he would be the oldest person ever to step into the presidency, a fact he’s determined to talk his way around. “Here’s a woman — she’s supposed to fight all of these different things, and she can’t make it 15 feet to her car,” he told supporters at a recent rally in Pennsylvania. “She’s home resting right now.” He slackened his jaw and feigned stumbling across the stage, a dramatic re-enactment of the video that showed Clinton nearly collapsing from pneumonia in September. “Folks,” Trump announced, “we need stamina.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16firstwords/16mag-16firstwords-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s Really Behind Trump’s Obsession With Clinton’s ‘Stamina’?', 'kicker': 'First Words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Show of Strength', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hess, Amanda', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'English Language', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8f609e83-e523-5114-87dc-c2735637ebf9', 'word_count': 1277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8f609e83-e523-5114-87dc-c2735637ebf9'}, {'abstract': 'A 1980 defeat set in motion a process of endless revision, by herself and her opponents, that has defined her career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/magazine/how-hillary-clinton-became-hillary.html', 'snippet': 'A 1980 defeat set in motion a process of endless revision, by herself and her opponents, that has defined her career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Two weeks after Hillary Clinton accepted the Democratic nomination for president, I flew to Little Rock, Ark., to visit a woman named Gay White. White is the widow of Frank White, a conservative Little Rock banker who in the spring, summer and fall of 1980 toured all 75 counties in Arkansas in a quixotic attempt to unseat the incumbent governor, Bill Clinton. Frank had no previous experience campaigning, but he proved to be an enthusiastic retail politician. Gay, then 32, accompanied him on his statewide tour of cattle auctions, courthouse squares, Walmart parking lots and chicken-processing plants. “Hi, I’m Gay White,” she would tell the people they met. “My husband’s running for governor, and I’d sure appreciate your vote.”', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '46', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16clintonoppo/16mag-16clintonoppo-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 896, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16clintonoppo/16mag-16clintonoppo-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 896}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16clintonoppo/16mag-16clintonoppo-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 686, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16clintonoppo/16mag-16clintonoppo-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1372, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16clintonoppo/16mag-16clintonoppo-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS