aph': 'WASHINGTON — In an argument marked by testy exchanges, the Supreme Court on Tuesday struggled to decide whether it should make an exception to the usual rule that jury deliberations are secret when evidence emerges that those discussions were marred by racial or ethnic bias.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12scotus/12scotus-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Supreme Court Weighs Bias and Secrecy in Jury Deliberations', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Court Mulls Jury Secrecy When Bias Is Revealed', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Jury System', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Discrimination', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sixth Amendment (US Constitution)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Colorado', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mexican-Americans', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Roberts, John G Jr', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sotomayor, Sonia', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T20:39:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Adam Liptak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Adam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Liptak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ee86520-601a-58a1-9d12-16834f68c873', 'word_count': 675, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ee86520-601a-58a1-9d12-16834f68c873'}, {'abstract': 'Stephen Jones, the British hatmaker who collaborates with the likes of Thom Browne and Rei Kawakubo, explains the appeal of top hats.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/11/t-magazine/fashion/stephen-jones-milliner-hats-video.html', 'snippet': 'Stephen Jones, the British hatmaker who collaborates with the likes of Thom Browne and Rei Kawakubo, explains the appeal of top hats.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This season alone, Stephen Jones created hats for Christopher Kane (retro pieces in the shape of collapsed cones), Thom Browne (oversized animal heads), Anya Hindmarch (bandage-esque headbands) and Maria Grazia Chirui’s much-anticipated debut at Dior (sporty visors). The milliner also collaborated with the young London College of Fashion graduate Ryan Lo on marabou-trimmed tricorn hats, which recalled the swashbuckling styles John Galliano used on his Dior runways during his reign from 1996 to 2011 (which Jones also created). Today, Galliano helms Maison Margiela — and while the house’s collaborators and contributors are kept secret, let’s just say this season featured some irreverent skull caps and headsets on the runway.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'In the Studio With One of Fashion’s Most Prolific Milliners', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hats and Caps', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Stephen (1957- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T20:50:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Fashion & Beauty', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lou Stoppard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lou', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stoppard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/605f789f-4122-576d-8582-52c03db84111', 'word_count': 600, 'uri': 'nyt://article/605f789f-4122-576d-8582-52c03db84111'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Pascal and Anthony Rapp, who starred in the original Broadway cast, team up to pay tribute to musical theater’s relationship with modern pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/12/arts/music/adam-pascal-anthony-rapp-review.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Pascal and Anthony Rapp, who starred in the original Broadway cast, team up to pay tribute to musical theater’s relationship with modern pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among the many moments when Broadway show music and modern pop have bowed and curtsied to one another, Jonathan Larson’s score for “Rent” is arguably the flash point when they fell into each other’s arms and sealed a partnership that continues to this day. I know, I know; as far back as “Hair,” there were successful hybrids. But the “Rent” juggernaut signaled a generational shift and locked a merger whose success has had everything to do with a younger generation of performers weaned on rock and schooled in musical theater.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/arts/12PASCAL/12PASCAL-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘Acoustically Speaking,’ a ‘Rent’ Duo Returns', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Rent’ Duo Pays Tribute to the Partnership of Show Music and Pop', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pascal, Adam', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rapp, Anthony', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Rent (Play)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Feinstein's/54 Below (Manhattan, NY, Music Venue)", 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T20:54:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stephen Holden', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stephen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Holden', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0eab4cb3-5db4-5bb2-ac96-84507d1a4a5b', 'word_count': 407, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0eab4cb3-5db4-5bb2-ac96-84507d1a4a5b'}, {'abstract': 'At Mr. Trump’s rallies, the candidate and the crowds draw energy and affirmation from one another, while dismissing any discouraging information.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/12/us/politics/donald-trump-voters.html', 'snippet': 'At Mr. Trump’s rallies, the candidate and the crowds draw energy and affirmation from one another, while dismissing any discouraging information.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WILKES-BARRE, Pa. — The line to see Donald J. Trump snaked back and forth on itself hours before his arrival. There was a carnival atmosphere with people in costumes, including one prison-striped man with a sign, “Don’t let the government-run media elect crooked Hillary.” A cavalcade of motorcycles roared up, and there were cheers and laughter for a man shouting, “Donald Trump is going to make America great! He hasn’t paid taxes in 20 years!”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 326}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 556, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/12/us/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1/12TRUMPDIEHARDS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1113, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Faltering? Die-Hard Fans Refuse to Buy It', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Sliding? Die-Hard Fans Refuse to Buy It', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gabriel, Trip', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pennsylvania', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-11T21:07:58+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Trip Gabriel', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Trip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gabriel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/47a728db-0e4c-57f5-bf4c-713c44fc1368', 'word_count': 1292, 'uri': 'nyt://article/47a728db-0e4c-57f5-bf4c-713c44fc1368'}, {'abstract': 'The Russian president suggested that athletes who require therapeutic use exemptions be barred from competing against those who do not.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/12/sports/vladimir-putin-russia-doping.html', 'snippet': 'The Russian president suggested that athletes who require therapeutic use exemptions be barred from competing against those who do not.', 'lead_paragraph': 'President Vladimir V. Putin of Russia waded into the nuances of antidoping protocols in sports on Tuesday, criticizing the practice of allowing athletes to use prohibited drugs for legitimate medical reasons. He claimed that athletes given such waivers had an unfair advantage.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multim