ne', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Casey Schwartz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Casey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwartz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0134df4f-c7e9-5f6f-b4b4-598918b38b80', 'word_count': 4785, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0134df4f-c7e9-5f6f-b4b4-598918b38b80'}, {'abstract': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on who is hurt when you bend the truth for a small personal gain, whether the punishment for breaking a resolution should ever be giving money to an organization you abhor and more.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/magazine/can-a-woman-pretend-to-be-a-lesbian-to-get-a-couples-discount.html', 'snippet': 'The magazine’s Ethicist columnist on who is hurt when you bend the truth for a small personal gain, whether the punishment for breaking a resolution should ever be giving money to an organization you abhor and more.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My local pool offers memberships for single people, couples (defined as “significant others living together”) and family memberships. The couples and family memberships are discounted from the rates for single people. I am a woman married to a man. I wanted to join this pool, but my husband was not interested, so a female friend and I joined as a “couple” to obtain the discounted rate. On the application, I described my female friend as my “partner” and listed her address as my address.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 961}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/magazine/16ethicist/16ethicist-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1100, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Can a Woman Pretend to Be a Lesbian to Get a Couples’ Discount?', 'kicker': 'The Ethicist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can I Pretend to Be a Lesbian to Get a Couples Discount?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Abuse, Rights and Welfare', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Appiah, Kwame Anthony', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethics (Personal)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philanthropy', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychology and Psychologists', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ethicist, The (Times Column)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subj