weather-bureau.html', 'snippet': 'Foreign intelligence copied “an unknown quantity of documents,” a government report said, but it did not specify which country may have been responsible.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Australia said on Wednesday that a foreign intelligence service had hacked into the country’s meteorology bureau last year, copying “an unknown quantity of documents” from its computer system.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Australia Says Foreign Spies Hacked Into Its Weather Bureau Last Year', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Australia', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cyberwarfare and Defense', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Espionage and Intelligence Services', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bureau of Meteorology (Australia)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-12T11:51:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Australia', 'byline': {'original': 'By Katie Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Katie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/03d2c807-e720-50a5-9f47-d5ce79333488', 'word_count': 176, 'uri': 'nyt://article/03d2c807-e720-50a5-9f47-d5ce79333488'}, {'abstract': 'Marriott recently acquired Starwood Hotels & Resorts, prompting questions about using the brands’ loyalty points. Here is what you need to know.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/travel/how-loyalty-programs-will-work-after-marriott-starwood-deal.html', 'snippet': 'Marriott recently acquired Starwood Hotels & Resorts, prompting questions about using the brands’ loyalty points. Here is what you need to know.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As executive vice president and chief marketing and commercial officer for Marriott International, Stephanie Linnartz oversees everything from technology to sales across the Marriott portfolio of hotels. In late September, that portfolio grew to 30 hotel brands from 19 when Marriott acquired Starwood Hotels & Resorts in a $13 billion deal that makes Marriott the largest hotel company in the world, managing over 5,700 hotels and 1.1 million rooms.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 796, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 796}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 772, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/travel/16QNA2/16QNA2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1543, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumb