rt to love, and slowly begins to accept himself for who he is.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/14/movies/the-david-dance-review.html', 'snippet': 'Troubled by insecurity, the host of a radio show opens his heart to love, and slowly begins to accept himself for who he is.', 'lead_paragraph': '“The David Dance” traces choreography in which a man steps closer to himself, then away; closer to love, then away again. Struggling with insecurity, David (Don Scimé) usually retreats from commitment. But on the airwaves, as the host of a gay radio show in Buffalo, he finds a clear, brave voice.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘The David Dance,’ a Gay Man Sheds His Crippling Self-Doubt', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The David Dance (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Winney, Aprill', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scime, Don', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-13T21:13:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Helen T. Verongos', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Helen', 'middlename': 'T.', 'lastname': 'Verongos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dd35c65-2625-5835-a98a-a83efc027fa8', 'word_count': 298, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dd35c65-2625-5835-a98a-a83efc027fa8'}, {'abstract': 'Charles LeDray, Lillian Schwartz, Hans-Peter Feldmann and a group of artists whose works are based on Fritz Lang’s film “Scarlet Street” are among the new exhibitions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/14/arts/design/what-to-see-in-new-york-ga