n New York Galleries This Week', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art in Review', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feldmann, Hans-Peter', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LeDray, Charles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schwartz, Lillian (1927- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Scarlet Street (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lang, Fritz', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-13T21:14:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Holland Cotter, Martha Schwendener and Will Heinrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Holland', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cotter', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Martha', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schwendener', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Will', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Heinrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0342ca83-541f-5e77-a190-d2bb1741bcd1', 'word_count': 1093, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0342ca83-541f-5e77-a190-d2bb1741bcd1'}, {'abstract': '“I’m a poet, I know it, hope I don’t blow it,” he once sang. He hasn’t.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/14/opinion/bob-dylan-master-of-change.html', 'snippet': '“I’m a poet, I know it, hope I don’t blow it,” he once sang. He hasn’t.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The hero of Don DeLillo’s 1973 novel, “Great Jones Street,” Bucky Wunderlick, is a wildly famous musician so transparently inspired by Bob Dylan that it is a wonder the author was able to make the figure into his own character. Bucky — part prophet, part fraud — is hounded into seclusion by fans, hustlers, gangsters and the world at large. I had a hunch Mr. DeLillo would win the Nobel Prize for Literature this year; he can’t be surprised Bob Dylan did.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14marcusWeb/14marcusWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Bob Dylan, Master of Change', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bob Dylan, Master of Change', 'name': None,