': 'Not long ago, an astonishing book landed on my desk. It’s called “Confessions of a Born-Again Pagan” and it weighs in at an impressive 1,076 pages. The author is Anthony Kronman, the former dean of the Yale Law School.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 753}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 816, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1632, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/14/opinion/14brooksWeb/14brooksWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Beauty of Big Books', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Beauty of Big Books', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pagans and Paganism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Philosophy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion and Belief', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marx, Karl', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Whitman, Walt', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kronman, Anthony T', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-14T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Brooks', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brooks', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b4cb18a-cefe-56a7-99b5-6c854659b073', 'word_count': 845, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b4cb18a-cefe-56a7-99b5-6c854659b073'}, {'abstract': 'A former Colombian president who set the stage for peace talks with rebels holds the key to salvaging or thwarting the accord.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/14/opinion/the-man-blocking-peace-in-colombia.html', 'snippet': 'A former Colombian president who set the stage for peace talks with rebels holds the key to salvaging or thwarting the accord.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A history book about Colombia’s recent past would rightly credit former President Álvaro Uribe, who governed from 2002 to 2010, with setting the stage for peace negotiations with guerrilla groups by leading a crackdown on insurgents that drove them to the negotiating table. Yet, confoundingly, Mr. Uribe has emerged as the chief obstacle to a negotiated end to Colombia’s 52-year armed conflict.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'capti