sburg has also become something of a pop culture superstar in recent years, ever since an admiring law student nicknamed her Notorious R.B.G. (a riff on the rapper Notorious B.I.G.). The meme went viral, and now Ginsburg’s stern face and big glasses show up on tote bags, baby onesies and coffee mugs bearing slogans like “The Ruth Will Set You Free.” So when Gwen Ifill talked with her for PBS’s “NewsHour Bookshelf” this month, the first question involved Ginsburg’s newfound status as a folk hero. “It is utterly amazing,” Ginsburg said. “Of course I didn’t see it coming. .\u2008.\u2008. But I certainly was given a tremendous boost into the public arena by the Notorious R.B.G. When I was asked about it, I said, well, it’s exactly right, because Notorious B.I.G. and I had something in common. .\u2008.\u2008. We were both born and bred in Brooklyn.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/books/review/23inside-list/23inside-list-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/books/review/23inside-list/23inside-list-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/books/review/23inside-list/23inside-list-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/books/review/23inside-list/23inside-list-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 270, 'width': 265, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/books/review/23insi