rd', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16JOINT1/16JOINT1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16JOINT1/16JOINT1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16JOINT1/16JOINT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16JOINT1/16JOINT1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16JOINT1/16JOINT1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16JOINT1/16JOINT1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Morso’s Modern Family: Five Years Old, but Decades in the Making', 'kicker': 'Neighborhood Joint', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond the Food, a Sense of Famiglia', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Sutton Place (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Morso (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Luongo, Pino', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-14T18:27:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Shivani Vora', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Shivani', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vora', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ed4f2f4e-0067-53ba-8944-5ad34f54c6b1', 'word_count': 573, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ed4f2f4e-0067-53ba-8944-5ad34f54c6b1'}, {'abstract': 'Regulators want to eliminate risk at Wall Street banks, and that will have unintended consequences – like higher interest rates — for everyone else.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/15/business/dealbook/how-wall-st-regulation-pushed-up-libor-and-borrowing-costs.html', 'snippet': 'Regulators want to eliminate risk at Wall Street banks, and that will have unintended consequences – like higher interest rates — for everyone else.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Is there any significance to the fact that a short-term interest rate has nearly tripled in the last year, to 0.86 percent from 0.32 percent? The short answer, of course, is yes. But the more interesting answer involves what the change in the so-called three-month London Interbank Offered Rate, or Libor, says about the Federal Reserve’s new regulatory framework for Wall Street, which it has slowly but surely been rolling out since the worst days of the financial crisis eight years ago.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'How Wall St. Regulation Pushed Up Libor, and Borrowing Costs', 'kicker': 'Street Scene', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Financial Institutions Examination Council', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Tarullo, Daniel K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Libor (London Interbank Offered Rate)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-14T18:31:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By William D. Cohan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'William', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e11928e-8bbc-516f-ac21-5331b79899a3', 'word_count': 1117, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e11928e-8bbc-516f-ac21-5331b79899a3'}, {'abstract': 'Mr. Trump attacked the women accusing him of inappropriate sexual advances, while claiming that the news media and Hillary Clinton were conspiring against him.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/15/us/politics/donald-trump-campaign.html', 'snippet': 'Mr. Trump attacked the women accusing him of inappropriate sexual advances, while claiming that the news media and Hillary Clinton were conspiring against him.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Donald J. Trump wielded his presidential candidacy on Friday as a weapon for savaging detractors and venting personal grievances, attacking the women who have accused him of sexual assault and unwelcome advances and railing against what he described as a vast conspiracy against him by the news media and Hillary Clinton’s campaign.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Donald Trump Assails His Accusers as Liars, and Unattractive', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump Alleges Vast Conspiracy Behind Accusers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Corasaniti, Nick', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Burns, Alexander', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value'