0-14T18:37:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Williams', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Williams', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a5195338-677e-589e-b1cc-1d941971e363', 'word_count': 549, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a5195338-677e-589e-b1cc-1d941971e363'}, {'abstract': 'For this high-achieving couple, the quiet of the day makes it a great time to work on music for four or five hours.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/nyregion/how-julia-wolfe-and-michael-gordon-bang-on-a-can-spend-their-sundays.html', 'snippet': 'For this high-achieving couple, the quiet of the day makes it a great time to work on music for four or five hours.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Julia Wolfe and Michael Gordon are two of the three founders and artistic directors of Bang on a Can, the genre-bending musical collective that will turn 30 next year. They’re also a married couple who raised two children in their TriBeCa loft, a former Romanoff Caviar factory. The two compose loud music at either ends of the loft, which they share with their daughter, Yael, 20, and a cockapoo named River. Ms. Wolfe, 57, who goes by Julie, just won a MacArthur fellowship to go with her 2015 Pulitzer Prize for her oratorio “Anthracite Fields,” about coal mining in Pennsylvania. “Amplified,” a guitar quartet by Mr. Gordon, 60, is scheduled to be performed at the Brooklyn Academy of Music’s Next Wave festival in December. They are workaholics who observe the Jewish Sabbath.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 470, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 470}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1603, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/nyregion/16ROUTINE3/16ROUTINE3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How Julia Wolfe and Michael Gordon, Workaholic Composers, Spend Their Sundays', 'kicker': 'Sunday Routine', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Loft Life: Music, Stretching and Leftovers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gordon, Michael (1956- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Wolfe, Julia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bang on a Can', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-14T18:37:48+