dley, the first North American to manage in the Premier League, faces doubts, none of which were likely to abate after Swansea City‘s loss to Arsenal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — Just before the next act of his saga began, Bob Bradley took a few moments for himself.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 395, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 395}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 674, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/16/sports/soccer1/soccer1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 982, 'width': 1491, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Premier League Pioneer Reaches a Somewhat Hostile Destination', 'kicker': 'On Soccer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Trailblazer Reaches a Somewhat Hostile Destination', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Smith, Rory', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bradley, Bob (1958- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'English Premier League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Swansea City (Soccer Team)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Soccer', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Coaches and Managers', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-15T20:37:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Soccer', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rory Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rory', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0ba407aa-a3cb-50eb-9ccd-6a41cd2eb0eb', 'word_count': 999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0ba407aa-a3cb-50eb-9ccd-6a41cd2eb0eb'}, {'abstract': 'Even in a season where the length of games ticked up, Game 5 between the Dodgers and the Nationals stands out, taking 4 hours 32 minutes to complete.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/16/sports/baseball/length-of-a-game.html', 'snippet': 'Even in a season where the length of games ticked up, Game 5 between the Dodgers and the Nationals stands out, taking 4 hours 32 minutes to complete.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The Washington Nationals could be excused if they did not want to go home. Facing elimination on Thursday in Game 5 of their division series with the Los Angeles Dodgers, they did everything they could to stay alive, and ended up stretching a nine-inning game out to 4 hours 32 minutes.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'imag