ial-era buildings and decrepit homes claimed by squatters stand near new hotels in a neighborhood where trendiness and exclusivity portend gentrification. But the tug between the present and the past could just as easily apply to the area’s young gang members torn between old and new ways of survival while wondering if the remade district will have any room for them.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Gang Members Find a Future in a Historic Panama City Neighborhood', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gangs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Historic Buildings and Sites', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ornitz, Darren (Photographer)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Panama', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T08:00:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By David Gonzalez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonzalez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8464d100-1a7a-5c2d-bb4e-7606e7957a21', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8464d100-1a7a-5c2d-bb4e-7606e7957a21'}, {'abstract': 'Who is Sarah Frey and why is she adamant about her customers branching out to new uses for the pumpkins she grows?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/17/learning/questions-for-americas-pumpkin-queen-has-a-request-dont-carve-cook.html', 'snippet': 'Who is Sarah Frey and why is she adamant about her customers branching out to new uses for the pumpkins she grows?', 'lead_paragrap