age', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/17kaur-3-INYT/17kaur-3-INYT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Says You’re a Dane?', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Who says you’re a Dane?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration and Emigration', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refugees and Displaced Persons', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and Africa Migrant Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Copenhagen (Denmark)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T13:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ravinder Kaur', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ravinder', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaur', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3b879dd1-fe1c-591c-a0ae-9273984092ee', 'word_count': 949, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3b879dd1-fe1c-591c-a0ae-9273984092ee'}, {'abstract': 'In America we had swigged beer and spoken of withholding our votes, but people in other countries had walked it like we talked it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/18/opinion/they-say-they-want-a-revolution.html', 'snippet': 'In America we had swigged beer and spoken of withholding our votes, but people in other countries had walked it like we talked it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — I don’t have an ideological view of Karl Marx. Sometimes he is right, sometimes wrong, sometimes both at the same time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'They Say They Want a Revolution', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'They talk about a revolution', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Third-Party Politics (US)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'McGuinness, Martin', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T14:01:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Goldfarb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldfarb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7c8bf5ec-7b9c-5048-bca5-b56c69cf740e', 'word_count': 1002, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7c8bf5ec-7b9c-5048-bca5-b56c69cf740e'}, {'abstract': 'It’s the politics, stupid.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/17/distrust-of-data/', 'snippet': 'It’s the politics, stupid.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Like Claudia Sahm, I was struck by polling results indicating that around half of Trump supporters completely distrust official data — although maybe a bit less surprised, since I’ve been living in that world for years. In particular, the failure of high inflation to materialize led quite a few people on the right side of the political spectrum — including the likes of Niall Ferguson — to insist that the numbers were being cooked, so this is neither a new phenomenon nor one restricted to Trump types.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/101716krugman1/101716krugman1-articleLarge.png', 'height': 182, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/101716krugman1/101716krugman1-articleLarge.png', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 182}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/101716krugman1/101716krugman1-jumbo.png', 'height': 244, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/101716krugman1/101716krugman1-superJumbo.png', 'height': 244, 'width': 805, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/17/opinion/101716krugman1/101716k