44297f0cb', 'word_count': 217, 'uri': 'nyt://article/83032c48-bc98-5c97-b956-11f44297f0cb'}, {'abstract': 'A platter of corned beef, pastrami and other deli sandwich favorites is now available nationwide from Katz’s Delicatessen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/19/dining/katz-deli-meat-platter.html', 'snippet': 'A platter of corned beef, pastrami and other deli sandwich favorites is now available nationwide from Katz’s Delicatessen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'They say it feeds six to eight; I’d say a few more. Either way, it’s a pregame feast of New York deli specialties: corned beef, pastrami, Swiss cheese and rye bread, all sliced and ready to pile into sandwiches, with condiments and pickles included. Pigs in blankets and salami, too. The package is shipped for two-day delivery: Katz’s Delicatessen Game Day Package, $175, katzsdelicatessen.com/game-day-package.html.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 491, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 491}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 839, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1677, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/dining/19BURNER-KATZ/19BURNER-KATZ-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Deli Feast for Football Fans', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Party: A Taste of Home  for Giants and Jets Fans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delicatessens', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Katz's Delicatessen (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Meat', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T17:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/e271fecb-bbac-59d0-8813-d891a247cffb', 'word_count': 64, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e271fecb-bbac-59d0-8813-d891a247cffb'}, {'abstract': 'The S.E.C. sued the Texas attorney general for securities fraud related to his role promoting Servergy, a tech company, but a judge rejected the agency’s claims.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/18/business/dealbook/the-shadowy-line-between-friendly-sales-pitch-and-deception.html', 'snippet': 'The S.E.C. sued the Texas attorney general for securities fraud related to his role promoting Servergy, a tech company, but a judge rejected the agency’s claims.', 'lead_paragraph': 'When a friend or business acquaintance pitches an investment as a surefire winner, there can be a question about when that cajoling crosses over from mere sales talk to fraud. A recent case in Texas involving the state’s attorney general, Ken Paxton, shows finding that line can be difficult.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 417, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 417}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/business/18DB-WHITEcollar-web/18DB-WHITEcollar-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1423, 'width'