imes', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/science/18TOMATO/18TOMATO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Refrigerators, Tomatoes Lose Flavor at the Genetic Level', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'COld Truth: Keep Tomatoes Out of the Fridge', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tomatoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Refrigerators', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Klee, Harry J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Temperature', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T19:56:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By JoAnna Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/872b55a8-72f8-53c8-96d3-560d096eb84e', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/872b55a8-72f8-53c8-96d3-560d096eb84e'}, {'abstract': 'While there’s diplomatic momentum on addressing climate change, analysts warn of a big reality gap if the hope is actually stopping global warming.', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/17/todays-climate-progress-and-tomorrows-climate-challenges/', 'snippet': 'While there’s diplomatic momentum on addressing climate change, analysts warn of a big reality gap if the hope is actually stopping global warming.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Tracking recent headlines, you might think the world is finally\xa0on a\xa0path toward controlling global warming. On Saturday, diplomats announced a\xa0new international agreement aimed at phasing out a family of climate-warming compounds called hydrofluorocarbons, or HFCs. And earlier this month an agreement was reached to start curbing the climate impact from aviation and enough countries formally accepted the Paris Agreement on climate change to set it on a path to take legal force on Nov. 4.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/13/world/13Aircon-web2/13Aircon-web2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/13/world/13Aircon-web2/13Ai