 'type_of_material': '', '_id': 'nyt://audio/dbba0def-a3e4-5bc0-8c89-c80fa65d6a8f', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://audio/dbba0def-a3e4-5bc0-8c89-c80fa65d6a8f'}, {'abstract': 'This novel by Hakan Gunday is a vivid tour of the nightmares endured by refugees headed to Europe, told by a young smuggler who learns to exploit them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/18/books/review-in-more-dispatches-from-hell-by-a-human-trafficker.html', 'snippet': 'This novel by Hakan Gunday is a vivid tour of the nightmares endured by refugees headed to Europe, told by a young smuggler who learns to exploit them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This disturbing new novel by Hakan Gunday, one of Turkey’s leading young writers, is like a visit to a Hieronymus Bosch hell: terrifying scenes of suffering, starvation, sadism, depravity and the agonies associated with combat zones. “More” recounts the story of a boy named Gaza who works with his father, a human trafficker, and it conveys the suffering of refugees and migrants as they try to make their way from war-torn countries like Afghanistan and Syria through Turkey and eventually on to Greece and the wider world (that is, if they survive a cascade of perils, one more awful than the next). It is also the narrator’s coming-of-age story, starting at 9 — a dark fable that traces the metamorphosis of a bright schoolboy into an appalling monster.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 876, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 876}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 702, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/arts/18BOOKGUNDAY/18BOOKGUNDAY-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1454, 'width': 996, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: In ‘More,’ Dispatches From Hell by a Human Trafficker', 'kicker': 'Books of The Times', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Refugee Hell, the Trafficker’s Perspective', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gunday, Hakan (1976- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'More (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T21:06:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michiko Kakutani', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michiko', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kakutani', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/16faf495-7cc0-5897-81a7-f88d96bd2713', 'word_count': 770, 'uri': 'nyt://article/16faf495-7cc0-5897-81a7-f88d96bd2713'}, {'abstract': 'Notables gather at Carnegie Hall to pay tribute to the photographer, who died in June at age 87.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/18/fashion/remembering-bill-cunningham.html', 'snippet': 'Notables gather at Carnegie Hall to pay tribute to the photographer, who died in June at age 87.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March 2010, when the film “Bill Cunningham New York” had its premiere at the Museum of Modern Art, the subject of the film — the longtime New York Times photographer Bill Cunningham — stood outside on the West 53rd Street sidewalk, snapping photos of attendees as they strode into the theater. But he never went inside to the screening itself, and he always maintained that he had never seen the documentary that made him famous.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Remembering Bill Cunningham', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Photographer Remembered as ‘the Eyes of New York’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Emmrich, Stuart', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cunningham, Bill', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Carnegie Hall', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-17T21:20:16+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Stuart Emmrich', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Stuart', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Emmrich', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/516b7653-2936-59e0-9152-a07f86ca73e5', 'word_c