-blue-jays-fans-rowdy-behavior.html', 'snippet': 'A can of beer was thrown toward an Orioles outfielder during Toronto’s home victory in the American League wild-card game, and racial abuse of two Orioles players was also reported.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TORONTO — In 2016 the Toronto Blue Jays enjoyed, by far, the largest attendance increase in Major League Baseball. In what was a natural result of last year’s riveting playoff run by the club, almost 600,000 additional fans poured through the turnstiles at Rogers Centre, leaving the Blue Jays with the third-highest attendance figure in the majors this season, behind only the Los Angeles Dodgers and the St. Louis Cardinals.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/sports/18fans1/18fans1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/18/sports/18fans1/18fans1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/sports/18fans1/18fans1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/sports/18fans1/18fans1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 733, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/18/sports/18fans1/18fans1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 733}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/18/sports/18fans1/18fans1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 838, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'su