fbb28e-0de7-57fc-bc51-24961770c5af'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Montparnasse tower in Paris is under development in October 1966.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/19/1966-500-foot-skyscraper-for-montparnasse/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Montparnasse tower in Paris is under development in October 1966.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — American and French businessmen are teaming up to build a skyscraper in Paris that they claim will be the world’s biggest — and most expensive — commercial building. At slightly more than 500 feet high, it would also be the highest building in central Paris. It would cost $100 million and stand on the site of the old Maine-Montparnasse railroad station. Plans for the new Paris landmark include a 250-room hotel, several restaurants and boutiques, a theater, an ice-skating rink, a heliport on the roof and underground parking and, inside the building, 30 high-speed elevators.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/blogs/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/20/blogs/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/blogs/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/blogs/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse/20oldiht-1966-montparnasse-jumbo.jpg', 'heig