word_count': 867, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f37bb299-2c77-5a90-93bd-5bc19744b300'}, {'abstract': 'Coming up: Art openings for Mark Leckey, Kerry James Marshall and Pipilotti Rist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/arts/design/big-bigger-and-biggest-in-museum-shows.html', 'snippet': 'Coming up: Art openings for Mark Leckey, Kerry James Marshall and Pipilotti Rist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s a great week to be in New York, especially if big, freshly-minted museum shows appeal. Things get rolling Sunday, Oct. 23, with the unveiling at MoMA PS1 of “Mark Leckey: Containers and Their Drivers,” the largest survey yet of this astute, often amusing perpetuator of video, installation, lecture-performance and photography. On Tuesday, the Met Breuer will debut “Kerry James Marshall: Mastry,” a survey of an artist whose ravishing, nuanced paintings confront the realities and history of black life in America. Wednesday brings “Pipilotti Rist: Pixel Forest,” a survey of a pioneering artist known for combining music and images of nature and the female body into some of contemporary art’s most lyrical videos and video installations. And Friday is the Whitney Museum’s turn with “Dreamlands: Immersive Cinema and Art, 1905-2016,” an expansive survey of a century-long relationship that will further explore the potential of the museum’s grand fifth-floor gallery.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 451, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 451}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1538, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23WEEKAHEAD9/23WEEKAHEAD9-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Big, Bigger and Biggest in Museum Shows', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Art; Big, Bigger and Biggest', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MoMA PS1', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Leckey, Mark (1964- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Met Breuer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Marshall, Kerry James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rist, Pipilotti', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Whitney Museum of American Art', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dreamlands: Immersive Cinema and Art, 1905-2016 (Exhibit)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-19T14:29:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roberta Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roberta', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/1f6a3d06-469f-53e7-aae7-a1a566c77d88', 'word_count': 149, 'uri': 'nyt://article/1f6a3d06-469f-53e7-aae7-a1a566c77d88'}, {'abstract': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Council-General of Paris decides to get rid of the pollution in the Reiver Seine from Asnières to Suresnes in October 1891.', 'web_url': 'https://iht-retrospective.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/19/1891-pollution-of-the-seine/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: The Council-General of Paris decides to get rid of the pollution in the Reiver Seine from Asnières to Suresnes in October 1891.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Dwellers in Paris, who, during the dry months of the year, are forced to drink Seine water or none at all, will be gratified to hear that a scheme for purifying the river, proposed six years ago, but abandoned on account of the cost, has been taken up again. The Council-General now proposes to divert all the sewer water that flows into the Seine and the Marne above Paris, convey it as far as Asnières, and there pump it up into a reservoir, whence it can be conducted on to the irrigation grounds at Achères. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/blogs/19oldiht-1891-seineriver/19oldiht-1891-seineriver-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/19/blogs/19oldiht-1891-seineriver/19oldiht-1891-seineriver-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight'