remist group.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/19/opinion/all-the-victims-of-boko-haram.html', 'snippet': 'The release of 21 kidnapped girls was both a joyous occasion and a sign of how much more it will take to defeat the extremist group.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The liberation of 21 of the more than 270 girls abducted from a Nigerian school in April 2014 is certainly to be celebrated. Yet, those heartwarming scenes of parents and girls joyously dancing and hugging are not the end of this terrible saga — not for the children still in the clutches of Boko Haram, the extremist Islamist group that has been spreading death and destruction across northeastern Nigeria for seven years, and perhaps not even for the girls who have been set free.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20thuBOKO/20thuBOKO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20thuBOKO/20thuBOKO-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20thuBOKO/20thuBOKO-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20thuBOKO/20thuBOKO-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 413, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20thuBOKO/20thuBOKO-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 413}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20thuBOKO/20thuBOKO-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 704, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo'