 tend to have costlier terms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/20/your-money/understanding-the-terms-of-your-student-loans.html', 'snippet': 'A new report finds that students aren’t borrowing the federal limit before seeking private or state loans, which tend to have costlier terms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As student debt for new graduates continues to climb, borrowers need to pay close attention to the type and the terms of the loans they seek, even if the loans come from state programs, a new report finds.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Understanding the Terms of Your Student Loans', 'kicker': 'Your Money Adviser', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Colleges and Universities', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Student Loans', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Federal Aid (US)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Finances', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Institute for College Access and Success', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'College Scorecard (Web Site)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-19T20:26:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ann Carrns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ann', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Carrns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/66b1a3cd-978c-50d5-bfad-c922d251c4fa', 'word_count': 615, 'uri': 'nyt://article/66b1a3cd-978c-50d5-bfad-c922d251c4fa'}, {'abstract': 'A special education preschool program based in Queens was treated as the personal ATM of the family that owns it, according to an agreement with the state attorney general’s office.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/20/nyregion/education-company-to-repay-4-3-million-in-settlement-with-new-york-state.html', 'snippet': 'A special education preschool program based in Queens was treated as the personal ATM of the family that owns it, according to an agreement with the state attorney general’s office.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A for-profit network of schools and the family behind it have agreed to pay New York State more than $4.3 million in a settlement after having spent state funds, intended to pay for special education preschool, on credit card bills, maintenance of a boat and a son’s law school tuition, as well as claiming false tax deductions, the office of the state attorney general, Eric T. Schneiderman, said on Wednesday.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/nyregion/20settlement1/20settlement1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/20/nyregion/20settlement1/20settlement1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/nyregion/20settlement1/20settlement1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/nyregion/20settlement1/20settlement1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/20/nyregion/20settlement1/20settlement1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/201