, renowned for its ceramics since the 15th century.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/10/19/t-magazine/the-centuries-old-ceramics-techniques-of-faenza.html', 'snippet': 'The artist Emma Hart’s Max Mara Prize residency has taken her to the Italian city, renowned for its ceramics since the 15th century.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Emma Hart’s Max Mara Prize residency has taken her to the Italian city, renowned for its ceramics since the 15th century.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 416, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 416}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 711, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1421, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM/19tmag-hart-slide-0SAM-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Centuries-Old Ceramics Techniques of Faenza', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-19T20:31:49+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/62506e25-1202-5791-8ce7-3bff7799210a', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/62506e25-1202-5791-8ce7-3bff7799210a'}, {'abstract': 'As the Max Mara Prize winner Emma Hart reaches the end of a residency there, she takes T on a tour of workshops keeping an ancient ceramic tradition alive.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/19/t-magazine/art/emma-hart-ceramics-faenza-italy.html', 'snippet': 'As the Max Mara Prize winner Emma Hart reaches the end of a residency there, she takes T on a tour of workshops keeping an ancient ceramic tradition alive.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The artist Emma Hart is not a fan of the glossy, filtered visions of life offered by Instagram, at least as most people use it. Though she has a background in photography, Hart has issues with the medium’s tendency to make subjects look “good and smooth,” and favors instead a pursuit of the grubby and real. Her artworks draw on the vexations of modern life with mischievous humor, referencing ill-paid jobs in call centers, faceless bureaucracy, the travails of young motherhood and her own South London roots.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/19/t-magazine/19tmag-hart-slide-EB7I/19tmag-hart-s