ons', 'value': 'Max Mara', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-19T20:31:52+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'subsection_name': 'Art', 'byline': {'original': 'By Hettie Judah', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Hettie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Judah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/493af3e3-9f40-5754-9b6f-bac3ca8ad322', 'word_count': 676, 'uri': 'nyt://article/493af3e3-9f40-5754-9b6f-bac3ca8ad322'}, {'abstract': 'We gave handwriting samples from five playwrights to a graphologist. Here’s what she saw, and how the writers reacted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/theater/they-write-plays-for-a-living-but-hows-their-handwriting.html', 'snippet': 'We gave handwriting samples from five playwrights to a graphologist. Here’s what she saw, and how the writers reacted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The brochure for the Playwrights Horizons season features the word “Playwrights” written eight times, by each of the featured theatermakers (seven writers and a collaborating director). The concept was to create a look that “would never be the same twice,” said Michael Bierut, a partner in the design firm Pentagram, which created a new brand identity for the Off Broadway company.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23HANDWRITING11/23HANDWRITING11-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23HANDWRITING11/23HANDWRITING11-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/arts/23HAND