urioso’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Ferrara (Italy)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Orlando Furioso: 500 Years (Exhibit)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T04:01:23+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SpecialSections', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': 'By Roderick Conway Morris', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Roderick', 'middlename': 'Conway', 'lastname': 'Morris', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/26869eed-3a4e-5d2b-8864-9fd1c6d4503a', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/26869eed-3a4e-5d2b-8864-9fd1c6d4503a'}, {'abstract': 'The Van Gogh Museum in Amsterdam traces Daubigny’s artistic development and the Impressionist painters he inspired.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/20/arts/design/van-gogh-museum-traces-daubigny-influence.html', 'snippet': 'The Van Gogh Museum in Amsterdam traces Daubigny’s artistic development and the Impressionist painters he inspired.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In July 1890, about 10 days before Vincent van Gogh shot himself in the chest, he presented his just-completed “Daubigny’s Garden” to the widow of a French landscape painter he had long admired, Charles-François Daubigny.', 'print_section': 'S', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/arts/20RARTDAUBIGNY-inyt1/20RARTDAUBIGNY-inyt1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 326, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'image