igrant Crisis', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AMNESTY INTERNATIONAL', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Immigration Detention', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T07:21:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/68899181-4d55-57af-a6c5-20874a655ada', 'word_count': 484, 'uri': 'nyt://article/68899181-4d55-57af-a6c5-20874a655ada'}, {'abstract': 'The American in me recognizes that we need to take care of Americans first.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/20/opinion/how-to-vote-as-an-immigrant-and-a-citizen.html', 'snippet': 'The American in me recognizes that we need to take care of Americans first.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Are you a citizen?” the woman standing in front of my apartment building in Manhattan asked me this summer. She had a clipboard with a sign-up sheet in one hand, which she extended to me as I walked toward her. “I’m looking for registered voters who would like to sign a petition to ——” I took the clipboard before she was done explaining. “Are you an American?” she asked again. Smiling, I unhooked a pen as I told her, “Yes, I’m an American.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20mbueWeb/20mbueWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 359, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20mbueWeb/20mbueWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 359}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/opinion/20mbueWeb/20mbueWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 612, 'width': 1024, 'subTyp