{'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Every Hidden Thing (Book)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppel, Kenneth (1967- )', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Chelsey Philpot', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Chelsey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Philpot', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/14e302d1-e42a-5b0e-a0e9-4ac431a43875', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/14e302d1-e42a-5b0e-a0e9-4ac431a43875'}, {'abstract': 'You can take a breath and escape physically and metaphysically, occupying and occupied by the music.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/magazine/letter-of-recommendation-choir.html', 'snippet': 'You can take a breath and escape physically and metaphysically, occupying and occupied by the music.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I sang in my college’s church choir every Sunday despite the occasional hangover. All that echo! The resounding nave wrung my heart out harder and better than any of the desiccated marijuana, clumsily mixed drinks or inept gropings of the nights before. We were Mormons and Baptists, Protestants who knew the Anglican hymns, Catholics who could translate the Latin, closeted baritones who were planning careers in music or the church or both.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/magazine/23lor/23mag-23lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/magazine/23lor/23mag-23lor-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}