 document.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To describe “Moonlight,” Barry Jenkins’s second feature, as a movie about growing up poor, black and gay would be accurate enough. It would also not be wrong to call it a movie about drug abuse, mass incarceration and school violence. But those classifications are also inadequate, so much as to be downright misleading. It would be truer to the mood and spirit of this breathtaking film to say that it’s about teaching a child to swim, about cooking a meal for an old friend, about the feeling of sand on skin and the sound of waves on a darkened beach, about first kisses and lingering regrets. Based on the play “In Moonlight Black Boys Look Blue” by Tarell Alvin McCraney, “Moonlight” is both a disarmingly, at times almost unbearably personal film and an urgent social document, a hard look at American reality and a poem written in light, music and vivid human faces.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-superJumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/arts/21MOONLIGHT/21MOONLIGHT-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Moonlight’: Is This the Year’s Best Movie?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Boyhood to Manhood: Poor, Black and Gay', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Moonlight (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jenkins, Barry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hibbert, Alex', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Ashton', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rhodes, Trevante', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T15:59:39+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/b701e36d-50a8-56c6-80e2-a209600dfa5f', 'word_count': 1281, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b701e36d-50a8-56c6-80e2-a209600dfa5f'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s premium YouTube service carries a monthly subscription fee, but you get more videos and fewer ads with your membership.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/21/technology/personaltech/what-youtube-red-gives-you-for-10-a-month.html', 'snippet': 'Google’s premium YouTube service carries a monthly subscription fee, but you get more videos and fewer ads with your membership.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. What does the paid version of YouTube offer? Do you get better video streaming than on the free site?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'What YouTube Red Gives You for $10 a Month', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Video Recordings, Downloads and Streaming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'YouTube.com', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T16:18:49+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/0034bd2c-7e0d-574a-b785-0b93c7c1979d', 'word_count': 300, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0034bd2c-7e0d-574a-b785-0b93c7c1979d'}, {'abstract': 'An employer weighs hiring a Trump supporter, while another urges her staff to vote for Clinton. Where to go for some peace? (Apparently not the dog run.)', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/fashion/social-qs-politics-donald-trump-hillary-clinton-office-etiquette.html', 'snippet': 'An employer weighs hiring a Trump supporter, while another urges her staff to vote for Clinton. Where to go for some peace? (Apparently not the dog run.)', 'lead_paragraph': 'I own a small bakery that’s taking off. (We make a crazy good coconut cake!) I put a sign in the window, looking for help, and asked the manager to set up interviews with the best candidates. On the morning of the interviews, I saw a woman park her car. It had a Trump bumper sticker on it. By coincidence, she turned out to be the first person I interviewed. How terrible would it be for me not to hire her on that basis alone? If it makes a difference, I am an American citizen, born here, but my mom is Mexican. I have felt attacked by Mr. Trump.', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 923, 'width': 925, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbStandard-v3.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2011/07/28/fashion/social_inline/social_inline-thumbLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Workplace Politics (the Trump-Clinton Kind)', 'kicker': 'Social Q’s', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Workplace Politics', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Careers and Professions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hiring and Promotion', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Customs, Etiquette and Manners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T16:19:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Philip Galanes', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Philip', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Galanes', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8224d09d-40fb-52f7-9048-2e6c1974f6f1', 'word_count': 854, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8224d09d-40fb-52f7-9048-2e6c1974f6f1'}, {'abstract': 'Do the moderators of the presidential debates deserve scorn for leaving out climate change?', 'web_url': 'https://dotearth.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/20/climate-silence-goes-way-beyond-debate-moderators/', 'snippet': 'Do the moderators of the presidential debates deserve scorn for leaving out climate change?', 'lead_paragraph': 'With three presidential debates and one for vice president behind us, David Leonhardt posted a helpful tally of debate questions — decrying the lack of a single question on one of the key issues facing humanity in this century and beyond: human-driven climate change. (The issue was touched on twice by Hillary Clinton in answers to other questions.)', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multime