31b1e-9d47-565b-a422-b194f88889fa'}, {'abstract': 'A $7.50-an-hour job at Kroger is a long way from Dodger Stadium.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/21/sports/baseball/andrew-toles-los-angeles-dodgers-nlcs.html', 'snippet': 'A $7.50-an-hour job at Kroger is a long way from Dodger Stadium.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — The experience gap in the Dodgers’ starting lineup for its two National League Championship Series victories over the Chicago Cubs was so vast, the fleet-footed outfielder Andrew Toles would have a hard time covering it. On one end was Toles, in his fourth month in the majors, in left field. At the other was second baseman Chase Utley, who is in his 14th season. The Dodgers’ manager, Dave Roberts, said he liked the seasoning mix because all of his players, young and old, were tough.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/sports/20TOLESweb1/20TOLESweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/20/sports/20TOLESweb1/20TOLESweb1-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/sports/20TOLESweb1/20TOLESweb1-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/sports/20TOLESweb1/20TOLESweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/20/sports/20TOLESweb1/20TOLESweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': Non