s protuberant eyes were fixed cruelly on his New York subjects. His voluptuous lips were set in steely resolve. Towering on a marble base above the Bowling Green, the gilded equestrian statue of King George III evoked a Roman emperor. With right arm upraised over the heads of the rabble, his message to a colony in revolutionary turmoil was plain enough: Don’t even think about it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/21/nyregion/21statue1/21statue1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Long-Toppled Statue of King George III to Ride Again, From a Brooklyn Studio', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Long-Toppled Statue of King George III Will Ride Again', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'George III, King of England (1738-1820)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'StudioEIS', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Revolutionary War, American (1775-83)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Museum of the American Revolution', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New-York Historical Society', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Models and Replicas', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-20T17:40:59+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4aa74a2b-b167-52c0-8086-5943b6844736', 'word_count': 966, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4aa74a2b-b167-52c0-8086-5943b6844736'}, {'abstract': 'Originally a state-owned table-tennis footwear brand, Startas ceased production because of Croatia’s war of independence. Now, it’s ready for a comeback.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/startas-sneakers-croatia-relaunch.html', 'snippet': 'Originally a state-owned table-tennis footwear brand, Startas ceased production because of Croatia’s war of independence. Now, it’s ready for a comeback.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You couldn’t buy Coca-Cola, but you could buy a bottle of Cockta, which is from Slovenia, and which I still love,” says the Croatian-American entrepreneur Robert Grgurev, recalling his childhood in the former Yugoslavia. Similarly, circa 1976, in lieu of Western sneakers like Converse and Superga, Croatia introduced Startas. The state-owned table-tennis footwear brand sponsored the 1987 World University Games in Zagreb; according to Grgurev, who is now the brand’s US-based president, “Every cool older kid or college student had at least one pair.” That is, until the 1990s, when production came to a brutal halt during Croatia’s war of independence, in which the one-industry town of Vukovar — home of the company’s headquarters — was ground zero.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-startas-01/20tmag-startas-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-startas-01/20tmag-startas-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-startas-01/20tmag-startas-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-startas-01/20tmag-startas-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 300, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-startas-01/20tmag-startas-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 300}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/20/t-magazine/fashion/20tmag-startas-01/20tmag-startas-01-jumbo.jp