iginal': 'By Jaime Joyce', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaime', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Joyce', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b6304776-48e8-5a41-97cb-affa7869ea01', 'word_count': 609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b6304776-48e8-5a41-97cb-affa7869ea01'}, {'abstract': 'A 403(b) plan is similar to the more familiar 401(k), but it is subject to less stringent securities regulations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/your-money/403-b-retirement-plans-explained.html', 'snippet': 'A 403(b) plan is similar to the more familiar 401(k), but it is subject to less stringent securities regulations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The so-called 403(b) plans are tax-deferred workplace retirement investment accounts, which are similar in many ways to their more widely used counterparts, 401(k) plans.', 'print_section': 'BU', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Answers to Questions About 403(b) Plans', 'kicker': 'Public Sacrifice', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Answers to Questions About 403(b) Plans', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bernard, Tara Siegel', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': '401(k), 403(b) and 457 Plans', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pensions and Retirement Plans', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stocks and Bonds', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Series', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-21T20:41:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'SundayBusiness', 'section_name': 'Your Money', 'byline': {'original': 'By Tara Siegel Bernard', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Tara', 'middlename': 'Siegel', 'lastname': 'Bernard', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0bfa53a3-5f57-56fc-a773-a64486622d93', 'word_count': 351, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0bfa53a3-5f57-56fc-a773-a64486622d93'}, {'abstract': 'To make it easier to sift through data on proteins, a composer and a biologist turned them into music, an approach that could have many applications.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/22/science/proteins-music.html', 'snippet': 'To make it easier to sift through data on proteins, a composer and a biologist turned them into music, an approach that could have many applications.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is your Friday cryptography problem: There are about 100,000 different kinds of proteins in the human body, each made out of different combinations of amino acids. They are the building blocks of life. When something goes wrong in our body’s mini-machinery and botches the shape of some proteins, they can’t do their job.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Studying the Building Blocks of Life in Stereo Sound', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Melody Maker: Want to Identify Proteins? Just Listen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Proteins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'DNA (Deoxyribonucleic Acid)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Heliyon (Journal)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bywater, Robert P', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Middleton, Jonathan N (1967- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-21T20:48:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joanna Klein', 'person': [{'first