aption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/23sun1web/23sun1web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1472, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/23sun1web/23sun1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/23sun1web/23sun1web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/23sun1web/23sun1web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chance to Unseat Marco Rubio', 'kicker': 'Hot Seats', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Chance to Unseat Marco Rubio', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rubio, Marco', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Murphy, Patrick Erin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hispanic-Americans', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-22T18:30:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/c738d427-af98-5daa-8556-78cfeff3275d', 'word_count': 621, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c738d427-af98-5daa-8556-78cfeff3275d'}, {'abstract': 'To get things done in Washington, you sometimes have to be a hypocrite.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/opinion/campaign-stops/why-hillary-clinton-needs-to-be-two-faced.html', 'snippet': 'To get things done in Washington, you sometimes have to be a hypocrite.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Although this year’s presidential race has not been a season of gentle ironies, there’s one to be found in the revelation of what are alleged to be Hillary Clinton’s closed-door speeches. After all the fuss about the bombshells they might contain, they show a warmer and more relaxed figure than the guarded, elusive and sometimes evasive persona she presents to the public.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 480, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 480}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 819, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23rauch/23rauch-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 1350, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Hillary Clinton Needs to Be Two-Faced', 'kicker': 'Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Why Hillary Clinton Needs to Be Two-Faced', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rauch, Jonathan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Speeches and Statements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-22T18:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Campaign Stops', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jonathan Rauch', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jonathan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Rauch', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b77b200-f012-558d-a0dd-d659ce28f1d1', 'word_count': 1115, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b77b200-f012-558d-a0dd-d659ce28f1d1'}, {'abstract': 'Even as he got seriously ill, my father’s mind was on work.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/the-books-my-dad-wont-read-mine.html', 'snippet': 'Even as he got seriously ill, my father’s mind was on work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Last November, a week after I had last seen him, my father passed out while sweeping the driveway (he’s the kind of man who sweeps the driveway, the kind of man who thinks something like passing out is caused by either having had too much coffee or not enough coffee), and within 24 hours of being admitted to the emergency room, he was told he had leukemia. The doctors said that, without treatment, he had about six weeks to live. He was 58.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 423, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 423}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 722, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 1951, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/opinion/sunday/26capo-crucet-inyt/23capo-crucet-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Books My Dad Won’t Read? Mine', 'kicker': 'Contributing Op-Ed Writer', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'It’s O.K., Don’t Read My Books', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Crucet, Jennine Capo', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Death and Dying', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Leukemia', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-22T18:30:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennine Capó Crucet', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennine', 'middlename': 'Capó', 'lastname': 'Crucet', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/852039fa-4975-5e41-93f7-9c42bfa84fd5', 'word_count': 1227, 'uri': 'nyt://article/852039fa-4975-5e41-93f7-9c42bfa84fd5'}, {'abstract': 'Posthumously erasing convictions for gross indecency, sodomy and “crimes against nature” is a critical move in the right direction.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/britains-step-toward-justice-for-gay-men.html', 'snippet': 'Posthumously erasing convictions for gross indecency, sodomy and “crimes against nature” is a critical move in the right direction.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Britain’s decision to posthumously pardon the tens of thousands of gay men convicted of seeking or having sex is just and long overdue. But it is unjust that 15,000 men who were convicted before those laws were repealed and who are still alive will have to go through an onerous process of applying for a pardon.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 746, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 746}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 824, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1648, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23sun2/23sun2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain’s Step Toward Justice for Gay Men', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Britain’s Step Toward Justice for Gay Men', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Turing, Alan M', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Amnesties, Commutations and Pardons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-22T18:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/2db93f3f-43cd-5d93-b37f-a04abd06864d', 'word_count': 473, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2db93f3f-43cd-5d93-b37f-a04abd06864d'}, {'abstract': 'Donald Trump will continue ranting, but we can soon choose whether to listen.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/the-medias-moment-of-truth.html', 'snippet': 'Donald Trump will continue ranting, but we can soon choose whether to listen.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The media’s responsibility for Donald Trump’s political success will be debated for a good long while, with the network honcho Les Moonves’s words about Trump’s candidacy (“It may not be good for America, but it’s damn good for CBS”) front and center. But almost from the moment that Trump entered the 2016 presidential race, he has been a justifiably huge story. A lead in the polls became a lead in the delegate count and then, surreally, the nomination of the Republican Party.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 492, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 492}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 841, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23bruni/23bruni-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1681, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Media’s Moment of Truth', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Columnist', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Media’s Moment of Truth', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-22T18:30:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Frank Bruni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Frank', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bruni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3c6be3b3-6c1d-597d-bef3-3e947c370f04', 'word_count': 1098, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3c6be3b3-6c1d-597d-bef3-3e947c370f04'}, {'abstract': 'I lost a child, and yet I chose to become a father again. Is that bravery or stupidity?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/children-dont-always-live.html', 'snippet': 'I lost a child, and yet I chose to become a father again. Is that bravery or stupidity?', 'lead_paragraph': 'My daughter, Greta, was 2 years old when she died — or rather, when she was killed. A piece of masonry fell eight stories from an improperly maintained building and struck her in the head while she sat on a bench on the Upper West Side of Manhattan with her grandmother. No single agent set it on its path: It wasn’t knocked off scaffolding by the poorly placed heel of a construction worker, or fumbled from careless hands. Negligence, coupled with a series of bureaucratic failures, led it to simply sigh loose, a piece of impersonal calamity sent to rearrange the structure and meaning of our universe.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23greene/23greene-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 802, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23greene/23greene-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 802}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23greene/23greene-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 767, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/23/opinion/sunday/23greene/23greene-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1534, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name