nut Nystedt.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/24/arts/music/review-berlin-radio-choir-honors-bach-and-those-he-influenced.html', 'snippet': 'In the program “Immortal Bach,” part of the White Light Festival, the ensemble sang works by Heinrich Schütz, Bach, Brahms, Schoenberg and Knut Nystedt.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In recent years New Yorkers have gotten to know the members of the Berlin Radio Choir for their acting skills as much as for their extraordinary singing. In 2014 the ensemble performed in the director Peter Sellars’s theatrical staging of Bach’s “St. Matthew Passion” with the Berlin Philharmonic at the Park Avenue Armory. Recently the choir opened Lincoln Center’s White Light Festival with “Human Requiem,” a dramatized performance of Brahms’s German Requiem in which the choristers acted out the texts as they sang, while moving about and mingling with the audience.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/24IMMORTAL1/24IMMORTAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/24IMMORTAL1/24IMMORTAL1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/24IMMORTAL1/24IMMORTAL1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/24IMMORTAL1/24IMMORTAL1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/24IMMORTAL1/24IMMORTAL1-thumbStand