d-cr-r-uck-about.html', 'snippet': 'Just a decade ago, the birds were almost nowhere to be seen or heard in the city. Today, their numbers are growing, and they have been sighted nesting in parks and on buildings.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Crows and ravens would seem to be the perfect New Yorkers. Both bird species are whip-smart, sociable, energetic, talkative and loud. And they dress entirely in black.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 867, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 867}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 709, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/nyregion/24BIRD/24BIRD-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1955, 'width': 1353, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Crows and Ravens Make New York Comebacks to Caw (and Cr-r-ruck) About', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In City, Comebacks to Caw (and Cr-r-ruck) About', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crows (Birds)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Birds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'West Nile Virus', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parks and Other Recreation Areas', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-24T01:25:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By David W. Dunlap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Dunlap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d996029a-3d86-5e91-827c-65347a8a37ff', 'word_count': 824, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d996029a-3d86-5e91-827c-65347a8a37ff'}, {'abstract': 'Much of the concern about AT&T’s $85.4 billion purchase of Time Warner is rooted in how consumers have fared since Comcast bought NBCUniversal.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/24/business/dealbook/swift-opposition-to-resurrection-of-att-giant.html', 'snippet': 'Much of the concern about AT&T’s $85.4 billion purchase of Time Warner is rooted in how consumers have fared since Comcast bought NBCUniversal.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over three decades ago, such was AT&T’s monopoly over the nation’s communications networks that the government forcefully shattered its empire.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 488, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 488}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 832, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/business/24DB-MERGER/24DB-MERGER-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1665, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Swift Opposition to Resurrection of AT&T Giant', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Opposition Immediate and Wide to Resurrection of AT&T Giant', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AT&T Inc', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'de la Merced, Michael J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Time Warner Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Antitrust Laws and Competition Issues', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mergers, Acquisitions and Divestitures', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Telephones and Telecommunications', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cable Television', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-24T01:29:29+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'subsection_name': 'DealBook', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael J. de la Merced', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'J.', 'lastname': 'de la Merced', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2dc64e24-ba98-5ebc-992b-14d471729029', 'word_count': 1141, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2dc64e24-ba98-5ebc-992b-14d471729029'}, {'abstract': 'For wised-up androids like Maeve, freedom’s just another word for nothing left to lose.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/23/arts/television/season-1-episode-4-truth-and-consequences.html', 'snippet': 'For wised-up androids like Maeve, freedom’s just another word for nothing left to lose.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For visitors to the park, the chief allure of Westworld is freedom: freedom from the strictures of legality and social norms; freedom to indulge in whatever violent and sexual fantasies they can imagine; freedom of the kind settlers might have experienced in the wide-open terrain of the Old West, before civilization came along and posted the guardrails. The paradox of Westworld is that freedom isn’t possible, because the park is monitored more closely than Disneyland and the hosts are synthetic constructs, acting on their loops. Comparisons to “sandbox” video games like “Grand Theft Auto” are apt: Players may enjoy wandering around between missions, shooting at random passers-by and looking for “Easter eggs,” but they’re penned in by the limits of this heavily monitored world.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/arts/television/24westworld/24westworld-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Westworld’ Season 1, Episode 4: Truth and Consequences', 'kicker': 'Westworld', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Westworld (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-24T02:01:24+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 