nted the toque as part of the uniform. They’ve been documented in a book with a sampling of ink adorning the bodies of dozens of chefs, male and female, precisely drawn by Wendy MacNaughton. Pigs are very popular; John Prescott of Eden East in Austin, Tex., has one on his head. Some, like the bee behind the left ear of Angie Mar, the chef and an owner of the Beatrice Inn in Manhattan, are discreet: “Knives & Ink: Chefs and the Stories Behind Their Tattoos (With Recipes)” by Isaac Fitzgerald and Wendy MacNaughton (Bloomsbury, $24).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/dining/26BURNERBOOK/26BURNERBOOK-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/26/dining/26BURNERBOOK/26BURNERBOOK-thumbStandard-v4.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/dining/26BURNERBOOK/26BURNERBOOK-thumbLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/dining/26BURNERBOOK/26BURNERBOOK-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'height': 769, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/26/dining/26BURNERBOOK/26BURNERBOOK-articleLarge-v4.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 769}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/dining/26BURNERBOOK/26BURNERBOOK-jumbo-v4.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 799, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url'