_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-24T19:30:29+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'T Magazine', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/09c782cc-7604-5f66-bf20-fbd2ff934fc1', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/09c782cc-7604-5f66-bf20-fbd2ff934fc1'}, {'abstract': 'In the stark TriBeCa world of La Garçonne’s Kris Kim, beauty comes from knowing precisely when to stop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/24/t-magazine/fashion/kris-kim-la-garconne-moderne-home-store.html', 'snippet': 'In the stark TriBeCa world of La Garçonne’s Kris Kim, beauty comes from knowing precisely when to stop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'To be told you are making something out of nothing is to be criticized for being overly dramatic, and yet to make something lovely out of nothing, and with very little dramatic flourish, is a clever skill, and precisely what the entrepreneur Kris Kim does. You cannot recognize the designer behind the loose black T-shirt and flowing black linen pants she is wearing on a recent meeting, and that is how she likes it. In fact, she is the designer, and the pieces are from her label, Moderne, which she sells at her shop and 11-year-old commerce site, La Garçonne, as well as at other retailers. The Moderne line is so simple that inside the company it’s referred to as “the Nothing Label.”', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '70', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/25/t-magazine/25tmag-kriskim-slide-O65K/25tmag-kriskim-slide-O65K-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/25/t-magazine/25tmag-kriskim-slide-O65K/25tmag-kriskim-slide-O65K-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth':