lle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Innis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Mike', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ives', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a9b3c4ce-591e-5454-b924-c6e64be4e638', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a9b3c4ce-591e-5454-b924-c6e64be4e638'}, {'abstract': 'When a young Egyptian medical student’s dreams of democracy collapsed, he joined fellow expatriates in the United States, documenting their hopes for the future.', 'web_url': 'https://lens.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/25/after-egypts-revolution-a-new-start-in-american-exile/', 'snippet': 'When a young Egyptian medical student’s dreams of democracy collapsed, he joined fellow expatriates in the United States, documenting their hopes for the future.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I was a medical student and political activist when the revolution against the Mubarak regime in Egypt broke out in 2011. While studying in Alexandria, I assisted as a medic during clashes between demonstrators and government forces. A few days before the fall of Mubarak, a young man was shot dead while standing between my friend Hesham and me. We could not save him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'After Egypt’s Revolution, a New Start in American Exile', 'kicker': 'Lens', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Demonstrations, Protests, and Riots', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Egypt', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-25T08:00:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': '', 'section_name': 'Multimedia/Photos', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amr Alfiqy', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amr', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alfiqy', 'qualifier': None, 'tit