nk would make the better president of the United States?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/25/learning/who-do-you-want-to-win-the-2016-presidential-election.html', 'snippet': 'Who do you think would make the better president of the United States?', 'lead_paragraph': 'The presidential primaries, party conventions and televised debates are all over. In fact, early voting is already underway in many states. With only two weeks left until Election Day, we’re in the homestretch of what The Times has called “the most surreal presidential campaign in modern times.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/04/27/us/27xp-snapchat-LN/27xp-snapchat-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Who Do You Want to Win the 2016 Presidential Election?', 'kicker': 'Student Opinion', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-25T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Learning', 'section_name': 'The Learning Network', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael Gonchar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gonchar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f758ff36-61c6-5498-ae19-5081da20eb07', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f758ff36-61c6-5498-ae19-5081da20eb07'}, {'abstract': 'In this season’s true crime books, mysteries set in Indianapolis; Austin, Tex.; Louisiana; and elsewhere.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/books/review/notorious-mrs-clem-and-more-true-crime.html', 'snippet': 'In this season’s true crime books, mysteries set in Indianapolis; Austin, Tex.; Louisiana; and elsewhere.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not all true-crime books are created equal. Some explore the criminal mind. Others focus on the lives of the victims. And then there are the ones that look beyond the crime to the historical period and social conditions in which it’s rooted. But one thing can be said for them all: True crime is hardly ever boring.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/1030-BKS-TrueCrime-Stasio/1030-BKS-TrueCrime-Stasio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 421, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/3