uri': 'nyt://article/9104d63b-e079-5292-8fad-4d72a4b50fca'}, {'abstract': 'Capitol Crossing, a mixed-use development, will cover a feeder road to Washington freeways; plans call for moving a landmark synagogue.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/26/realestate/commercial/a-project-mends-a-gash-in-the-street-grid-of-washington.html', 'snippet': 'Capitol Crossing, a mixed-use development, will cover a feeder road to Washington freeways; plans call for moving a landmark synagogue.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — The depressed highway is a road from nowhere, the remnant of an Interstate once planned to cut through residential neighborhoods. Activists blocked the larger plan for the freeway in the 1960s, so this small segment close to the Capitol is left to feed traffic from city streets to other freeways, leading south over the Potomac to Virginia and east across the Anacostia River.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/business/26CAPITOLCROSSING1/26CAPITOLCROSSING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/26/business/26CAPITOLCROSSING1/26CAPITOLCROSSING1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/business/26CAPITOLCROSSING1/26CAPITOLCROSSING1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/business/26CAPITOLCROSSING1/26CAPITOLCROSSING1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/26/business/26CAPITOLCRO