 'Dan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Barry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fad2e746-cfc9-5db2-9a78-f6752a7bc750', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fad2e746-cfc9-5db2-9a78-f6752a7bc750'}, {'abstract': 'Sunday in Brooklyn and Samesa open in Williamsburg, the Wild Son opens beneath the High Line, and more restaurant news.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/26/dining/white-gold-butchers-from-april-bloomfield-opens-uptown.html', 'snippet': 'Sunday in Brooklyn and Samesa open in Williamsburg, the Wild Son opens beneath the High Line, and more restaurant news.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WHITE GOLD BUTCHERS Not long ago, the artisanal local butcher appeared to be going the way of the snow leopard. But a growing demand for alternatives to factory chickens and plastic packages of chuck steaks has inspired a butcher’s renaissance in many places. Now, Upper West Side carnivores can have their pastured beef, air-chilled poultry and heritage pork, along with charcuterie like head cheese, from the new meat market and restaurant that Ken Friedman and the chef April Bloomfield have bestowed on the neighborhood. About half the no-frills corner space is an open kitchen with display cases for the work of Erika Nakamura and Jocelyn Guest, the butchers. Items like rotisserie chicken can be brought home for dinner, but those tempted by a slab of pork terrine or a hot dog on the spot can perch at a counter and even accompany it with beer, wine or kombucha from a tap. Tufted black leather banquettes, tables and chairs furnish the restaurant portion, with counter service at breakfast and lunch, and waiters at dinner with a menu of items like lettuce wrap with crispy pork, hacked chicken with green sauce, smoked lamb ribs, and rice with drippings. (Butcher and takeout open Wednesday, restaurant opens Nov. 1): 375 Amsterdam Avenue (78th Street), whi