ew York City, but the lure of its signature barbecue sandwich was impossible to resist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I can tell you with complete assurance that 532 miles is not too far to travel for a sandwich. That is the distance between my home in Ridgewood, Queens, and the Skylight Inn in Ayden, N.C., where a man in a black apron fills the cutout between the kitchen and the cash register and wields cleavers as if they were weapons from “Game of Thrones,” one in each substantial hand. He stands above twin slabs of butcher block that were once flat but which now resemble dugout canoes, from decades of metronomic chopping. “We like to say our wood tastes better than most people’s meat,” one of the countermen said to me.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/travel/26SKYLIGHT/26SKYLIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 781, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/26/travel/26SKYLIGHT/26SKYLIGHT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 781}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/travel/26SKYLIGHT/26SKYLIGHT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 788, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/travel/26SKYLIGHT/26SKYLIGHT-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1575, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/travel/26SKYLIGHT/26SKYLIGHT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/26/travel/26SKYLIGHT/26SKYLIGHT-thumbStanda