: 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cleveland Indians', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chicago Cubs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-26T16:49:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By The New York Times', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The New York Times'}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/229dd719-3669-51d5-8a50-98b8dc3c3746', 'word_count': 78, 'uri': 'nyt://article/229dd719-3669-51d5-8a50-98b8dc3c3746'}, {'abstract': 'This gospel fest includes Fred Hammond, Karen Clark Sheard, Israel Houghton and the up-and-comer Casey J.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/arts/music/the-festival-of-praise-tour-arrives-in-brooklyn.html', 'snippet': 'This gospel fest includes Fred Hammond, Karen Clark Sheard, Israel Houghton and the up-and-comer Casey J.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This year’s installment of the annual Festival of Praise Tour, at Kings Theater in Brooklyn on Wednesday, Nov. 2, is strong on 1990s and early 2000s heavy hitters: Fred Hammond, with his buttery, tender voice; the off-the-cuff powerhouse Karen Clark Sheard; the versatile worship leader Israel Houghton. These are stars of gospel’s maximalist period and occasional flirters with its pop-soul instincts. But the lineup offers a couple of surprises at the margins, too: Regina Belle, a soul star of the 1980s and ’90s who has turned to gospel over the last decade; and the youngest singer on the bill, the up-and-comer Casey J, whose appealing take on gospel is more sonically modest and internally complicated than the lions she joins on this tour. (kingstheatre.com)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD4/30WEEKAHEAD4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Festival of Praise Tour Arrives in Brooklyn', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pop; Gospel Singers, Young and Old', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gospel Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hammond, Fred', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sheard, Karen Clark', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Houghton, Israel (1971- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Belle, Regina', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hobbs, Casey Janice (Casey J)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-26T16:50:37+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jon Caramanica', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jon', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Caramanica', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/54b7d939-8a90-5a94-b45d-8110f85df449', 'word_count': 124, 'uri': 'nyt://article/54b7d939-8a90-5a94-b45d-8110f85df449'}, {'abstract': 'Songs by Richard Rodgers, Mary Rodgers and Adam Guettel at Merkin Concert Hall, and compositions by Gabriela Lena Frank at National Sawdust.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/arts/music/at-the-classical-new-york-festival-of-song-music-for-deciding-a-vote.html', 'snippet': 'Songs by Richard Rodgers, Mary Rodgers and Adam Guettel at Merkin Concert Hall, and compositions by Gabriela Lena Frank at National Sawdust.', 'lead_paragraph': 'What does it mean to be American? As the election season lurches into its final stretch, the New York Festival of Song offers a chance to reflect on the question through music, and from different vantage points. On Tuesday, Nov. 1, and Thursday at Merkin Concert Hall, this cherished institution presents “Rodgers, Rodgers & Guettel: A Century of American Musical Theater,” a program that takes the temperature of the American dream as expressed in the songs by Richard Rodgers, his daughter Mary Rodgers (“Once Upon a Mattress”) and his grandson Adam Guettel (known for the score to “The Light in the Piazza”). The vibrant lineup includes the soprano Lauren Worsham, the mezzo-soprano Mary Testa and the baritone John Brancy. On Wednesday at National Sawdust, the organization’s new-music arm invites the Peruvian-American composer Gabriela Lena Frank to design an evening around her own folk-and-mythology-inspired compositions as well as works by the composers Avner Dorman and Derek Bermel. Performers include the soprano Amy Owens; the Momenta Quartet; and the festival’s associate artistic director, Michael Barrett, at the piano. (nyfos.org; nationalsawdust.org)', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30WEEKAHEAD1/30WEEKAHEAD1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'At the Classical New York Festival of Song, Music for Deciding a Vote', '