ideshow/ed1884a7-072e-56c3-a81b-9d138fb1f5ab'}, {'abstract': 'For 14 years, Ellen Koenigsberg’s throwback finds have served up inspiration to labels like Marc Jacobs and Maryam Nassir Zadeh.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/26/t-magazine/fashion/ellen-lower-east-side-nyc-vintage-store.html', 'snippet': 'For 14 years, Ellen Koenigsberg’s throwback finds have served up inspiration to labels like Marc Jacobs and Maryam Nassir Zadeh.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For 14 years, Ellen Koenigsberg has stocked her Lower East Side vintage shop, Ellen, with pieces that have served as inspiration for fashion labels like Marc Jacobs and Maryam Nassir Zadeh. “When I moved in, Brooklyn wasn’t an adjective and e-commerce didn’t really exist,” she says of her store’s first location, just across the street from her current one at 123 Ludlow. It was the summer of 2002 and only a handful of shops — like Marmalade, Foley and Corinna and TG-170 — existed. “They’re not here anymore, any of them,” she says sadly.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/t-magazine/fashion/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/26/t-magazine/fashion/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/t-magazine/fashion/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/t-magazine/fashion/ellen-konigsberg-slide-HAMF/ellen-konig