 'snippet': 'As part of a festival, a rural town in Connecticut played host to more than 1,300 devotees, who endured rain to tour the town and meet stars from the show.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON, Conn. — In 1999, a television writer named Amy Sherman-Palladino vacationed at the Mayflower Grace, a five-star inn built high on a hill here. In true Hollywood fashion, Ms. Sherman-Palladino returned to her hometown, Los Angeles, and from her brief visit spun Stars Hollow — a charming New England small town with its own resident troubadour. Stars Hollow would become the setting for “Gilmore Girls,” her cultishly popular mother-daughter dramedy that ran for seven seasons on the WB (and later the CW).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Fans Flock to Town That Inspired ‘Gilmore Girls’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Next Best Thing to Visiting ‘Gilmore Girls’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sherman-Palladino, Amy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Connecticut', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Gilmore Girls (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-26T21:04:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Styles', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steven Kurutz', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steven', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kurutz', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dabd70be-e275-5c0a-b725-a1fcb20b54a4', 'word_count': 1260, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dabd70be-e275-5c0a-b725-a1fcb20b54a4'}, {'abstract': 'The discovery of nine fossilized claw bones suggests that prehistoric humans may have decorated with animal skins.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/27/science/cave-lion-pelts-caverns.html', 'snippet': 'The discovery of nine fossilized claw bones suggests that prehistoric humans may have decorated with animal skins.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some 16,000 years ago, prehistoric humans ventured deep into the La Garma cave in Spain to perform sacred rituals. Guided by lanterns made of animal fat, they navigated hundreds of feet through dark caverns and around thick stalagmites until they reached one of their circular stone huts, each of which had a horse skull at its center.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/science/27TB-cavelion/27TB-cavelion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/27/science/27TB-cavelion/27TB-cavelion-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/science/27TB-cavelion/27TB-cavelion-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/science/27TB-cavelion/27TB-cavelion-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 350, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/27/science/27TB-cavelion/27TB-cavelion-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 350}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/science/27TB-cavelion/27TB-cavelion-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 598, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None