ior might not be President Kirkman, and that’s not necessarily a bad thing.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Welcome back to the White House! This week’s episode of “Designated Survivor” revolves around a military strike, and contains all the classic elements of the show we’ve come to know and (maybe) love: ominous lead-chasing, flirtatious-yet-strained banter, close-ups on widening eyes, thickly laid moral dilemmas. Most interestingly, it implicitly floats the idea that President Kirkman is not, in fact, the hero of this story.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/watching/26designatedsurvivor/26designatedsurvivor-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/26/watching/26designatedsurvivor/26designatedsurvivor-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/watching/26designatedsurvivor/26designatedsurvivor-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/watching/26designatedsurvivor/26designatedsurvivor-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/26/watching/26designatedsurvivor/26designatedsurvivor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/26/watching/26designatedsurvivor/26designatedsurvivor-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, '