on': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/0c9cc615-78ab-5a2b-a037-b50addd95ad5', 'word_count': 586, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0c9cc615-78ab-5a2b-a037-b50addd95ad5'}, {'abstract': 'Rereading William Golding’s classic, Lois Lowry finds herself despairing that circumstances led the children to such a hell.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/books/review/their-inner-beasts-lord-of-the-flies-six-decades-later.html', 'snippet': 'Rereading William Golding’s classic, Lois Lowry finds herself despairing that circumstances led the children to such a hell.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lord of the Flies” was published in 1954, the year that I turned 17, and I read it not long after. I was in the habit then (as I still am today) of finding, in each book I read, the fictional character with whom I identified — the one with whom I would travel. If you are new to this book, as I was then, you will meet Ralph right up front. I felt an immediate kinship with Ralph, even before I knew his name. He is the first character introduced, and for a few pages he is called only by his description: “the fair boy.” I could relate to that. I was also “fair,” which I took to mean blond, and, though I wouldn’t have thought this through at the time, I played fair. I followed the rules. It seemed Ralph did too.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 894}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 687, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1616, 'width': 1084, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/books/review/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE/30LOWRY-CRITICSTAKE-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Their Inner Beasts: ‘Lord of the Flies’ Six Decades Later', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Take', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Lord of the Flies’ 60 Years Later', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Golding, William', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Lord of the Flies (Book)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T09:00:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lois Lowry', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lois', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowry', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id'