ct': 'Trade and economic growth is making Beijing more repressive, not less.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/opinion/americas-dangerous-china-fantasy.html', 'snippet': 'Trade and economic growth is making Beijing more repressive, not less.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Throughout the 1990s and early 2000s, American business executives and political leaders of both parties repeatedly put forward what I label the “China fantasy”: the view that trade, foreign investment and increasing prosperity would lead to political liberalization in the world’s most populous country.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/opinion/28mann-inyt/28mann-inyt-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'America’s Dangerous ‘China Fantasy’', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'America’s dangerous ‘China fantasy’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'China', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Communist Party of China', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'International Trade and World Market', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T10:33:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Mann', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mann', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/6403eddb-9cb2-52f2-b77e-a683248f74b9', 'word_count': 896, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6403eddb-9cb2-52f2-b77e-a683248f74b9'}, {'abstract': 'It would be a mistake to imagine that the Democrats’ relative harmony is a permanent situation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/27/opinion/campaign-stops/can-liberals-all-just-get-along.html', 'snippet': 'It would be a mistake to imagine that the Democrats’ relative harmony is a permanent situation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This article is part of the Opinion Today newsletter. You can sign up here to receive more briefings and a guide to the section daily in your inbox.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/07/15/timestopics/sub2-leonhardt-topics/sub2-leonhardt-topics-article