ttos-broadway.html', 'snippet': 'Times have changed for gay rights, leading the makers of “Falsettos” to wonder how the show will be received compared with its Broadway debut in 1992.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1992, the musical “Falsettos” arrived on Broadway, bringing to the world’s biggest stage a self-centered nebbish named Marvin, who, having left his wife and son for another man, was nevertheless pining in song for “a tight-knit family” of “kid, wife and lover.” That year, Pat Robertson, at the Republican National Convention, was inveighing against Bill Clinton’s “radical plan to destroy the traditional family” and to “appoint homosexuals to his administration.”', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/arts/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1/30FALSETTOCOVERSUB1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1333, 'width': 2000, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An AIDS-Era Musical in an Age of Marriage Equality', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Will a Revival Still Resonate?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Theater', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schneier, Matthew', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Falsettos (Play)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Playwrights Horizons', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lapine, James', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Finn, William', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Borle, Christian', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rannells, Andrew', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Homosexuality and Bisexuality', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Acquired Immune Deficiency Syndrome', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T17:05:27+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Theater', 'byline': {'original': 'By Matthew Schneier', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Matthew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schneier', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf5b6fe4-d4e7-5f35-b095-0041a51f50c2', 'word_count': 1999, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf5b6fe4-d4e7-5f35-b095-0041a51f50c2'}, {'abstract': 'If Mozilla’s browser automatically calls up that stand-alone mail software you never use when you click a “mailto” link, here’s how to fix it.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/technology/personaltech/make-firefox-open-gmail-to-send-a-message.html', 'snippet': 'If Mozilla’s browser automatically calls up that stand-alone mail software you never use when you click a “mailto” link, here’s how to fix it.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Q. When I click an email address link on a web page to send a new message on my PC, Firefox tries to open the separate mail program I never use, instead of switching to the Gmail page I have open in another tab and creating the new message there. Can I fix this?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Make Firefox Open Gmail to Send a Message', 'kicker': 'Tech Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Web Browsers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T17:05:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'subsection_name': 'Personal Tech', 'byline': {'original': 'By J. D. Biersdorfer', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Question', '_id': 'nyt://article/2187c0e5-7218-5615-a874-bf667ab06bff', 'word_count': 289, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2187c0e5-7218-5615-a874-bf667ab06bff'}, {'abstract': 'Amazon’s new show, about a group of young journalists, has serendipitous parallels to the contentious gender politics dominating the presidential election.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/arts/television/review-in-good-girls-revolt-the-nasty-women-of-the-1960s-fight-job-discrimination.html', 'snippet': 'Amazon’s new show, about a group of young journalists, has serendipitous parallels to the contentio