idnight-movie-esque work from Jim Hosking.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Thank heavens Jim Hosking’s lurid live-action cartoon, “The Greasy Strangler,” found financing, because this oddity — borrowing liberally from a precious, vanishing institution, midnight movies — invites strong reactions. Yet its willful determination to be outré proves its undoing.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘The Greasy Strangler’ Pairs Father and Son in Tours and Gore', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hosking, Jim (Film Director)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T20:57:00+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andy Webster', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Webster', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7a5ef9f3-9323-5bc0-a4e9-254db9886e91', 'word_count': 243, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7a5ef9f3-9323-5bc0-a4e9-254db9886e91'}, {'abstract': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/briefing/asia-briefing.html', 'snippet': 'Here’s what you need to know to start your day.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/nytnow/28BRIEFING-asia-slide-243Z/28BRIEFING-asia-slide-243Z-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/27/nytnow/28BRIEFING-asia-slide-243Z/28BRIEFING-asia-slide-243Z-thumbStandard.