ealth/migraines-drugs-children.html', 'snippet': 'Researchers said it was clear that amitriptyline and topiramate hadn’t done better than a placebo. But some doctors were not ready to give up on drug treatment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Neither of the two drugs used most frequently to prevent migraines in children is more effective than a sugar pill, according to a study published on Thursday in The New England Journal of Medicine.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 403, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 403}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 688, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/science/28MIGRAINE/28MIGRAINE-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1375, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Two Drugs for Adult Migraines May Not Help Children', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Remedies For Migraine May Not Aid Young Much', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Migraine Headaches', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drugs (Pharmaceuticals)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Children and Childhood', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Journal of Medicine', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Powers, Scott W', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T21:14:25+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Catherine Saint Louis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Catherine', 'middlename': 'Saint', 'lastname': 'Louis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8b84091c-392d-5bc1-8455-f9ea17986d2f', 'word_count': 590, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8b84091c-392d-5bc1-8455-f9ea17986d2f'}, {'abstract': 'Aaron Biebert’s documentary argues that e-cigarettes could help smokers quit, if only powerful forces weren’t trying to discredit them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/movies/a-billion-lives-review.html', 'snippet': 'Aaron Biebert’s documentary argues that e-cigarettes could help smokers quit, if only powerful forces weren’t trying to discredit them.', 'lead_paragraph': '“A Billion Lives” is the kind of documentary that seeks to get you all worked up about an injustice but leaves you feeling as if there were nothing you could do about it. It’s also the kind of documentary that asks you to accept one set of experts’ version of things and reject another’s, when you suspect that disinterested parties are probably rare on either side.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘A Billion Lives’ Claims There’s a Conspiracy Against Vaping', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Smoking and Tobacco', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'A Billion Lives (Movie)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biebert, Aaron', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T21:15:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Neil Genzlinger', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Genzlinger', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/ee32eae8-9e72-5eef-ad85-3ecef1347229', 'word_count': 263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ee32eae8-9e72-5eef-ad85-3ecef1347229'}, {'abstract': 'There’s some great comedy and a not-bad doctor show airing tonight.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/watching/the-good-place-pure-genius-mom.html', 'snippet': 'There’s some great comedy and a not-bad doctor show airing tonight.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TV could use a new, good doctor show. “Pure Genius,” above, is not that. But it’s not all bad either, and given that it hails from Jason Katims, the executive producer of “Parenthood” and “Friday Night Lights,” hope springs eternal.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '16', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/24/watching/24watching2/24watching2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType'