/7ce851cf-29bf-5cb5-a3ae-44643f495704'}, {'abstract': 'Scenes from the Swiss artist’s video-centered show at the New Museum.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/slideshow/2016/10/28/arts/design/pipilotti-rist-pixel-forest.html', 'snippet': 'Scenes from the Swiss artist’s video-centered show at the New Museum.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Scenes from the Swiss artist’s video-centered show at the New Museum.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 899, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 899}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 684, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28RIST/28RIST-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1367, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Pipilotti Rist: Pixel Forest’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Art', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Rist, Pipilotti', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New Museum of Contemporary Art', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T21:25:00+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Arts', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Art & Design', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Slideshow', '_id': 'nyt://slideshow/e74ed3e1-24d2-5f73-9fae-0a5424b2c92e', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://slideshow/e74ed3e1-24d2-5f73-9fae-0a5424b2c92e'}, {'abstract': 'Werner Herzog’s documentary, a collaboration with a buoyant scientist, takes you to the precipice of volcanoes from Iceland to North Korea to Vanuatu.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/movies/into-the-inferno-review-werner-herzog.html', 'snippet': 'Werner Herzog’s documentary, a collaboration with a buoyant scientist, takes you to the precipice of volcanoes from Iceland to North Korea to Vanuatu.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Few filmmakers make the world seem more wondrous than Werner Herzog, more worthy of exploration and veneration. For decades, he has been probing the limits of existence, charting its mysteries and madness in fiction and nonfiction movies that together have created an extraordinary body of work. Part cinematic magus, part cosmic philosopher, he takes you places you never knew you wanted to go, asks questions you never considered and introduces you to characters who suggest the worst and the very best about us. There’s a strain of melancholia in this searching. I’m not sure if Mr. Herzog thinks that we can be saved — or are worth saving — but his restlessness suggests perhaps.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 319, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 319}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 544, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1088, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28INTOTHEINFERNO1/28INTOTHEINFERNO1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: ‘Into the Inferno,’ Staring Down the Terrors of Nature', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Staring Down the Terrors of Nature', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Volcanoes', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Herzog, Werner', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Into the Inferno (Movie)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Oppenheimer, Clive', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-27T21:28:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Manohla Dargis', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Manohla', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dargis', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/27f6e333-fc6a-51fa-a17a-ee2612efe890', 'word_count': 795, 'uri': 'nyt://article/27f6e333-fc6a-51fa-a17a-ee2612efe890'}, {'abstract': 'Jim Jarmusch’s reverent documentary on Iggy Pop, a provocateur, is prim: It includes no retrospective scenes of drug use or the bandmates’ fights.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/movies/gimme-danger-review-iggy-pop.html', 'snippet': 'Jim Jarmusch’s reverent documentary on Iggy Pop, a provocateur, is prim: It includes no retrospective scenes of drug use or the bandmates’ fights.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Considering the frenzied psychedelic circus it might have been, “Gimme Danger,” Jim Jarmusch’s reverent documentary portrait of Iggy Pop, one of rock’s ultimate daredevil provocateurs, is downright prim. There are casual confessions of self-destructive, out-of-control behavior by Iggy Pop and his band, the Stooges. But you don’t see it. You only hear about it, and it’s glossed over as yesterday’s bad-boy antics.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28GIMME/28GIMME-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 383, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28GIMME/28GIMME-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 383}}, {'