ector talks about his life and work.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Movies about great directors rarely live up to their subjects. Still, there are dividends. A documentary like “By Sidney Lumet,” for instance, gives you a chance to hang out with a favorite filmmaker, to listen to him talk about his life and work, to hear the cadences and occasional cracks in his voice. True, there are moments when you wish you were watching one of his movies instead, but there’s something to be said for a tribute that inspires you to revisit the films and again seek out “Long Day’s Journey Into Night,” “Serpico,” “Q&A” and his masterpiece, “Dog Day Afternoon.” (Mr. Lumet died in 2011 at 86.)', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28BYLUMET/28BYLUMET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28BYLUMET/28BYLUMET-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28BYLUMET/28BYLUMET-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28BYLUMET/28BYLUMET-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28BYLUMET/28BYLUMET-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/28BYLUMET/28BYLUMET-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype