 {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Dracula (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jason Zinoman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jason', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Zinoman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/9767d8b6-1b98-5baf-8a60-bfb400f743d4', 'word_count': 639, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9767d8b6-1b98-5baf-8a60-bfb400f743d4'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t stop pedaling. Use your arms to turn.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/magazine/how-to-ride-a-unicycle.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t stop pedaling. Use your arms to turn.', 'lead_paragraph': '“You’re going to fall a lot,” says Scott Wilton, vice president of the International Unicycling Federation. “It takes a long time to learn, and it takes the willingness to fall down and get back up.” Make sure the unicycle is the right size for you. Next, get on: “Stand behind the unicycle, not to the side of it like you would a bicycle,” Wilton says. Put the saddle between your legs and, with the pedal for your dominant foot at the 9 o’clock position, step up onto the unicycle as if you were climbing stairs; as the unicycle moves underneath you, put the other foot on its pedal. Hold onto a wall or a fence for support. (Dismounting is easy, Wilton says: “Step off backward — do the exact same thing you did to get on the unicycle, but in reverse.”)', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 961, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 961}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 640, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30tip/30mag-30tip-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1422, 'width': 888, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Ride a Unicycle', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Ride a Unicycle', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lowe, Jaime', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Unicycles', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jaime Lowe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jaime', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lowe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/af2ba117-e599-541e-a2c7-465a658dc7d0', 'word_count': 386, 'uri': 'nyt://article/af2ba117-e599-541e-a2c7-465a658dc7d0'}, {'abstract': 'A cocktail can help tap into our more indecorous desires.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/magazine/spirited-away.html', 'snippet': 'A cocktail can help tap into our more indecorous desires.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A couple of Halloweens ago, I decided to switch out my lazy, customary Frida Kahlo costume (thrown together in five minutes with an embroidered Mexican dress, a few dollar-store roses and an eyebrow pencil) and instead become Frida of the Damned, so I added stage blood and fangs to my usual get-up. I really tried to be scary.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '32', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30drink-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30drink-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30drink-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30mag-30drink-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 800, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30mag-30drink-t_CA1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 800}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30mag-30drink-t_CA1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 769, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/magazine/30drink-copy/30mag-30drink-t_CA1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1537, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Spirited Away', 'kicker': 'Drink', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Good Blood', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Schaap, Rosie', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cocktails and Mixed Drinks', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Whiskey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Halloween', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Recipes', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ALCOHOLIC BEVERAGES', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T09:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Rosie Schaap', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Rosie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Schaap', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a294944-bd4d-5cce-90b8-0c752319ac16', 'word_count': 472, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a294944-bd4d-5cce-90b8-0c752319ac16'}, {'abstract': 'Sometimes distance in a marriage can be a good thing. Especially when your husband seems to be impersonating the Tasmanian devil in his sleep.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/magazine/judge-john-hodgman-on-a-married-couples-bigger-bed.html', 'snippet': 'Sometimes distance in a marriage can be a good thing. Especially when your husband seems to be impersonating the Tasmanian devil in his sleep.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jeff writes: My wife and I sleep on an old full-size bed and are in need of a new one. I would like to buy another full because I am afraid i