None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8944675d-7ad6-5119-946e-40c140e813d1', 'word_count': 1054, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8944675d-7ad6-5119-946e-40c140e813d1'}, {'abstract': 'My grandfather’s family was all but wiped out in the Holocaust and I was the last person in my line to hold my family’s name.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/well/family/why-couldnt-i-give-my-child-my-last-name.html', 'snippet': 'My grandfather’s family was all but wiped out in the Holocaust and I was the last person in my line to hold my family’s name.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the mercury dipped below 30 degrees one night in my second trimester, my husband, Dave, and I ordered in Sichuan and started talking names. We wanted one that was classic, and to honor our families in some way. But we didn’t want to saddle our wee one with the Old World names that started appearing just a few branches up each of our family trees. Little Moshe, Yehuda and Golda had as much chance as did a Moon Unit, Apple or North.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 524, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 524}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 894, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1789, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/well/family/well-family-names/well-family-names-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Couldn’t I Give My Child My Last Name?', 'kicker': 'Ties', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Names, Personal', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Marriages', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Women's Rights", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T11:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Family', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sophie Brickman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sophie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Brickman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8622d90e-73a3-5640-b360-492989690704', 'word_count': 1050, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8622d90e-73a3-5640-b360-492989690704'}, {'abstract': 'It’s been an unusual presidential campaign season in many ways, and some of the ads are also a departure from established norms.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/29/upshot/ads-that-use-candidates-own-words-to-powerful-effect.html', 'snippet': 'It’s been an unusual presidential campaign season in many ways, and some of the ads are also a departure from established norms.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Hillary Clinton’s campaign released an ad in late September called “Mirrors.” The ad shows young girls looking carefully at themselves in a mirror or on their mobile phones. A piano tune accompanies the images. Then a surprising thing happens. Donald J. Trump, in his own voice, says, “I’d look her right in that fat, ugly face of hers. … She’s a slob, she ate like a pig. … A person who is flat-chested is very hard to be a 10. … Did she have a good body? No.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/upshot/28UP-ADS/28UP-ADS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/upshot/28UP-ADS/28UP-ADS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/upshot/28UP-ADS/28UP-ADS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/upshot/28UP-ADS/28UP-ADS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/upshot/28UP-ADS/28UP-ADS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/upshot/28UP-ADS/28UP-ADS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'l