 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc69591b-0c35-5ade-8998-3bbe95da2b2c'}, {'abstract': 'Older residents of the swing state, with the nation’s highest percentage of voters 65 and over, can only shake their heads about the bad manners on display in the 2016 race.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/29/us/florida-voters-2016-election.html', 'snippet': 'Older residents of the swing state, with the nation’s highest percentage of voters 65 and over, can only shake their heads about the bad manners on display in the 2016 race.', 'lead_paragraph': 'FORT MYERS, Fla. — Sixteen. That’s the number of times that Ellen Chrouch, a bird-loving Republican at the Shell Point Retirement Community here, has cast a vote for president, starting with Dwight D. Eisenhower in 1956 and, this year, a reluctant ballot for Donald J. Trump. During that time, America’s political landscape has been turned inside out and upside down, and to hear many older voters tell it, is now marked only by low roads.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/us/29florida1/29florida1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Florida Voters With the Longest Memories Don’t Like What They See', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Older Voters Carry Clout but Don’t Like the Choices', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Florida', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Alvarez, Lizette', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Retirement Communities and Assisted Living', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elderly', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T15:23:50+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Lizette Alvarez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Lizette', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Alvarez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/86974ac9-58e5-580c-a131-6c847373387d', 'word_count': 1170, 'uri': 'nyt://article/86974ac9-58e5-580c-a131-6c847373387d'}, {'abstract': 'Several exhibitions feature her works that skewer sociopolitical tendencies.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/29/arts/design/rachel-maclean-artist.html', 'snippet': 'Several exhibitions feature her works that skewer sociopolitical tendencies.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, England — Rachel Maclean makes for a dashing David Cameron. Dressed in a colonial pith helmet, ecclesiastical collar, camouflage-patterned kilt and prosthetic lion’s muzzle, the Scottish artist delivers one of the former prime minister’s more impassioned speeches as part of her 2014 video work “A Whole New World.” Behind her, the Union Flag flutters against an industrial wasteland bathed in preposterously tangerine CGI twilight.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/international/29maclean03-1INYT/29maclean03-1INYT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/international/29maclean03-1INYT/29maclean03-1INYT-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/international/29maclean03-1INYT/29maclean03-1INYT-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/international/29maclean03-1INYT/29maclean03-1INYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/international/29maclean03-1INYT/29maclean03-1INYT-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/international/29maclean03-1INYT/29maclean03-1INYT-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 10