 prevent the Buffalo Bills from securing a season sweep over the New England Patriots. Later Sunday, Green Bay Packers quarterback Aaron Rodgers and the Atlanta Falcons’ Matt Ryan will face off in what could be an epic shootout. But those veterans are merely a warm-up for the prime-time clash of two exciting rookie quarterbacks in a game with N.F.C. East implications:', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/sports/30MATCHUPSweb1/30MATCHUPSweb1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'N.F.L. Schedule: Here’s Who We Think Will Win in Week 8', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Prime Time  Could Be  Right Time  for Rookies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Football League', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T16:23:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Benjamin Hoffman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Benjamin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hoffman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/6336482a-5c43-5d0a-8443-cdcb80c80b85', 'word_count': 1447, 'uri': 'nyt://article/6336482a-5c43-5d0a-8443-cdcb80c80b85'}, {'abstract': 'A by-no-means exhaustive list of items we like.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/t-magazine/five-things-t-editors-are-really-into-right-now.html', 'snippet': 'A by-no-means exhaustive list of items we like.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The architect and designer Emilio Terry could have been a household name — he counted socialites and royalty among his clients, and Salvador Dalí and Jean-Michel Frank among his friends — if he hadn’t resisted publicity, preferring to fly under the radar. A new exhibition, “In Search of Emilio Terry,” fills in some of the blanks, combining his own work with pieces from his collection created by his influences and collaborators. The show is helped along with a big assist by T’s beloved contributing editor Konstantin Kakanias, who created a series of new paintings starring Mrs. Tependris, the fictional society doyenne he has been drawing for the last 20 years. On view through Nov. 12 at Eerdmans Fine Art, 14 E. 10th St., eerdmansfineart.com. — ALEXANDRIA SYMONDS', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/t-magazine/entertainment/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R/28tmag-editors-pics-slide-891R-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Five Things T Editors Are Really Into Right Now', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fashion and Apparel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Shoes and Boots', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Candles', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-28T16:23:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f6340e9-c7d4-5f5b-b802-86fe23e888ce', 'word_count': 551, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f6340e9-c7d4-5f5b-b802-86fe23e888ce'}, {'abstract': 'A crop of new restaurants goes beyond sushi, bringing hyperlocal specialties stateside.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/28/t-magazine/food/regional-japanese-cuisine-restaurants-ichiran-shibumi.html', 'snippet': 'A crop of new restaurants goes beyond sushi, bringing hyperlocal specialties stateside.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the States, we’ve tended to think of Japanese food as a single cuisine that includes raw fish, teriyaki, tempura and ramen. In Japan, as elsewhere, there are hyperlocal specialties: fried chicken in Nagoya, grilled oysters from Miyajima, tangerines and green tea in Shizuoka. Now, a crop of new restaurants is finally introducing some of this regional nuance to American diners. Ichiran, which opened last month in Brooklyn, has only one thing on the menu: tonkotsu ramen served Fukuoka-style, with straight, thin noodles and a rich pork-bone broth. TsuruTonTan in Manhattan specializes in udon from the Kansai region, served hot in a fish-based dashi or twisted over a bed of ice with a soy dipping sauce. Over in L.A., Shibumi offers kappo, a tradition in which the chef presents seasonal small plates — like Nagano-inspired fresh soba noodles in November — to diners at the counter.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '40', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/13/t-magazine/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0/13tmag-12look_food-t_CA0-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Regional Japanese Fare Comes to America', 'kicker': 'Food Matters', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Beyond Sushi: Regional Japanese Fare Comes to America', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'key