dlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2320cb1f-6814-5572-848a-de57a4450a6c', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2320cb1f-6814-5572-848a-de57a4450a6c'}, {'abstract': 'The de Blasio administration has explored the possibility of getting out of its contracts with the Trump Organization at Ferry Point, Wollman Rink and other sites.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/nyregion/blasting-out-of-a-trump-trap.html', 'snippet': 'The de Blasio administration has explored the possibility of getting out of its contracts with the Trump Organization at Ferry Point, Wollman Rink and other sites.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For anyone who predicted at the infancy of Donald J. Trump’s presidential bid — so many mean, vengeful, condemning, deranged remarks ago — that the unhinged nature his candidacy revealed would surely serve his business interests poorly, the past few weeks have delivered gratifying confirmation. Residents of a row of Trump buildings on Riverside Boulevard on the Upper West Side are rallying to have the Republican nominee’s name expunged from the facades. Simultaneously, protests have mounted against the United States Golf Association’s plan to hold the United States Women’s Open next year  at a Trump course in New Jersey, where it was scheduled four years ago, on the theory that holding it there would be like celebrating Earth Day in a pesticide factory.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/nyregion/30BIG/30BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/nyregion/30BIG/30BIG-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 