w York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Agreed: Serve Your Time, Cast Your Ballot', 'kicker': 'Editorial', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Agreed: Serve Your Time, Cast Your Ballot', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Ex-Convicts', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voting and Voters', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Editorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Voter Registration and Requirements', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Polls and Public Opinion', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-29T18:30:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Editorial', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By The Editorial Board', 'person': [], 'organization': 'The Editorial Board'}, 'type_of_material': 'Editorial', '_id': 'nyt://article/a377f0a5-1554-56cf-8880-d48b06ddd528', 'word_count': 136, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a377f0a5-1554-56cf-8880-d48b06ddd528'}, {'abstract': 'As systems for rating colleges multiply like mad, here’s a guide for consulting — and ignoring — them.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/opinion/sunday/how-to-make-sense-of-college-rankings.html', 'snippet': 'As systems for rating colleges multiply like mad, here’s a guide for consulting — and ignoring — them.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Willard Dix is one of the crankiest observers of the college admissions process I know; he’s also one of the smartest. He worked at Amherst, his alma mater, then advised college-bound students at a private secondary school in Chicago. He now blogs about higher education.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/opinion/sunday/30bru