tlyn Greenidge', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kaitlyn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenidge', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0e464805-9969-51d4-ae8e-6e5fb4b3323a', 'word_count': 1358, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0e464805-9969-51d4-ae8e-6e5fb4b3323a'}, {'abstract': 'Lawmakers have argued that an extra hour of afternoon sunlight would have social and health benefits and help the nation save millions on electricity.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/world/europe/spain-time-zone.html', 'snippet': 'Lawmakers have argued that an extra hour of afternoon sunlight would have social and health benefits and help the nation save millions on electricity.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MADRID — The Rodgers and Hart song “I Didn’t Know What Time It Was” has nothing to do with time zones, but it may soon resonate for many Spaniards.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Push to Tweak Time Zone Gains Momentum in Spain', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Push to Tweak Time Zone Gains Momentum in Spain', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Valencia (Spain)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Catalonia (Spain)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Europe', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Spain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Time', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Daylight Saving Time', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-29T18:30:47+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Raphael Minder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Raphael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Minder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/755fc45d-afe3-503f-9cc6-8835e4af0413', 'word_count': 476, 'uri': 'nyt://article/755fc45d-afe3-503f-9cc6-8835e4af0413'}, {'abstract': 'The tech billionaire is known for bucking convention, but his backing of Mr. Trump’s presidential bid has outraged much of Silicon Valley.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/31/technology/peter-thiel-defends-his-most-contrarian-move-yet-supporting-trump.html', 'snippet': 'The tech billionaire is known for bucking convention, but his backing of Mr. Trump’s presidential bid has outraged much of Silicon Valley.', 'lead_paragraph': 'SAN FRANCISCO — Peter Thiel likes to take the path not taken. He has paid students to drop out of college, thinks Silicon Valley is overrated, backed a plan to build cities on the high seas and helped propel an electronic form of money into general use. His contrarian approach to investing and to life has made him rich and celebrated.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Peter Thiel Defends His Most Contrarian Move Yet: Supporting Trump', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Peter Thiel, Contrarian Tech Billionaire, Defends His Support of Trump', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Streitfeld, David', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thiel, Peter A', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Silicon Valley (Calif)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Campaign Finance', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': '