'value': 'WikiLeaks', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-29T19:01:40+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Steve Eder and Nicholas Confessore', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Steve', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Eder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Confessore', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fe77abd-d9d0-50bc-8c1e-d1bfcbf3e068', 'word_count': 1248, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fe77abd-d9d0-50bc-8c1e-d1bfcbf3e068'}, {'abstract': 'She has been deranging conservatives since ’92, when wounded Republican invincibility merged with wounded male prerogative.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/opinion/sunday/how-hillary-clinton-met-satan.html', 'snippet': 'She has been deranging conservatives since ’92, when wounded Republican invincibility merged with wounded male prerogative.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It was my third day at the Republican National Convention in 1996, and my notebook overflowed with a one-note theme: “You do know that Hillary Clinton is funding the whole radical feminist agenda?” “She had Vince Foster killed.” “She’s behind many more murders than that.” “It’s well-established that Hillary Clinton belonged to a satanic cult, still does.” The consensus among Pat Buchanan’s supporters seemed ardent and universal, though the object of this obloquy wasn’t even on the opposing ticket.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/opinion/sunday/30faludi/30faludi-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbS