 {'abstract': 'Iraq’s Shiite militias aimed to take the city, a move that would essentially cut off the Islamic State fighters there from their bases in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/world/middleeast/tal-afar-iraq-isis.html', 'snippet': 'Iraq’s Shiite militias aimed to take the city, a move that would essentially cut off the Islamic State fighters there from their bases in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ERBIL, Iraq — The city of Tal Afar, a former Ottoman outpost not far from Mosul that has a mostly ethnic Turkmen population and has been home to a corps of Islamic State leaders, on Saturday became the focus of a growing struggle between Turkey and Iran for influence in northern Iraq.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/world/30IRAQ1/30IRAQ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/30/world/30IRAQ1/30IRAQ1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/world/30IRAQ1/30IRAQ1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/world/30IRAQ1/30IRAQ1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/world/30IRAQ1/30IRAQ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/world/30IRAQ1/30IRAQ1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 7