', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'South Africa', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-30T16:01:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicky Falkof', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicky', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Falkof', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/7effc4cd-af94-5ca9-8411-60b45fcb10f3', 'word_count': 1020, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7effc4cd-af94-5ca9-8411-60b45fcb10f3'}, {'abstract': 'In the campaign’s waning days, the disgraced congressman is at the center of the F.B.I.’s renewed interest in Hillary Clinton’s private email server.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/31/us/politics/anthony-weiner-democratic-reaction.html', 'snippet': 'In the campaign’s waning days, the disgraced congressman is at the center of the F.B.I.’s renewed interest in Hillary Clinton’s private email server.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carolyn B. Maloney, a congresswoman from the Upper East Side, was riding in a taxi on Friday when she heard the news: Emails discovered in an investigation into Anthony D. Weiner’s sexting had revived the F.B.I.’s interest in the case of Hillary Clinton’s private server.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/us/31WEINERDEMS/31WEINERDEMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/30/us/31WEINERDEMS/31WEINERDEMS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/30/us/31WEINERDEMS/31WEINERDEMS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150