 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/31/pageoneplus/no-corrections-october-31-2016.html', 'snippet': 'No corrections appeared in print on Monday, October 31, 2016.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No corrections appeared in print.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'No Corrections: October 31, 2016', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T01:06:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'NewsDesk', 'section_name': 'Corrections', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7948f724-ac8b-5457-9015-66317e86121a', 'word_count': 77, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7948f724-ac8b-5457-9015-66317e86121a'}, {'abstract': '“Never once,” Francona, the Indians manager, said. “You know why? I don’t care. I like what I’m doing.” Then he reconsidered.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/31/sports/baseball/terry-francona-legacy-cleveland-indians.html', 'snippet': '“Never once,” Francona, the Indians manager, said. “You know why? I don’t care. I like what I’m doing.” Then he reconsidered.', 'lead_paragraph': 'CHICAGO — Terry Francona ducked under a drain pipe and headed up the dank and narrow tunnel leading to the visitors’ clubhouse at Wrigley Field, the ancient baseball shrine. The clubhouse — any clubhouse — is his sanctuary, his favorite spot in the world, the place where he starts his day preparing for a game, well before his players arrive, so he can give them his full attention when they do.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/sports/baseball/31kepner/31kepner-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 375, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/31/sports/ba