, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/walkingdead2/walkingdead2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/28/arts/walkingdead2/walkingdead2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Walking Dead’ Season 7, Episode 2: Greetings From the Kingdom', 'kicker': 'The Walking Dead', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Walking Dead (TV Program)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T02:01:04+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy Egner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Egner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5fc8aa36-999c-5d61-8b02-edc9d7230d36', 'word_count': 1091, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5fc8aa36-999c-5d61-8b02-edc9d7230d36'}, {'abstract': 'Regardless of your theories, there is at least one thing that William and the Man in Black have in common.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/10/30/arts/television/westworld-season-1-episode-5-recap.html', 'snippet': 'Regardless of your theories, there is at least one thing that William and the Man in Black have in common.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The paradox of Westworld as a theme park is that guests come seeking a taste of freedom — no laws, no standards of decency, no limits beyond the horizon — but are, in fact, submitting themselves to a world that’s controlled, surveilled and quite literally programmed. It’s a fantasy of Old West freedom, and a potent one for thrill-seekers who give themselves over to it passively, chasing their animal desire for realistic shoot-‘em-ups and readily available android sex. But the more time spent in Westworld, the more the seams begin to show, and the behavioral patterns and loops start to look just as mundane and predictable as the domestic routines they’ve left behind.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/watching/30westworld/31westworld-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumb