016/10/31/1916-hindenburg-makes-boast-on-the-war/', 'snippet': 'From the archives of The International Herald Tribune: German Field Marshal von Hindenburg boasts about World War I and speculates on how long it might last, in October 1916.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Field-Marshal von Hindenburg has been interviewed at General Headquarters by a representative of the Vienna “Neue Freie Presse.” Questioned as to the military situation, he replied: “It is as favorable as possible, and everything will continue to go well.” “But how long will the war last?” asked the correspondent. “That depends on our adversaries,” said Hindenburg. “It is useless to prophesy. In war time especially, it is preferable to abstain from doing so. It is possible that the year 1917 may bring about fighting which will decide the war. I can say nothing as to this, but what I can say is that we shall never give in until a decision is reached.” ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/blogs/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 291, 'width': 385, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/blogs/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 291, 'width': 385, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/31/blogs/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/31/blogs/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg/31oldiht-1916-hindenburg-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None