zations', 'value': 'Federal Reserve System', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Economy', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T14:29:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Justin Fox', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Justin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fox', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/5741a888-966c-518d-9d5f-2bfc212315d9', 'word_count': 1245, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5741a888-966c-518d-9d5f-2bfc212315d9'}, {'abstract': 'Taking a break from the election to talk toy models.', 'web_url': 'https://krugman.blogs.nytimes.com/2016/10/31/trade-plateaus-wonkish/', 'snippet': 'Taking a break from the election to talk toy models.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Binyamin Appelbaum has a nice piece about the stall in world trade growth, which I (and many others) have been tracking for a while. And I thought I’d write a bit more about this, if only to serve as a much-needed distraction from the election.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Trade Plateaus (Wonkish)', 'kicker': 'Paul Krugman', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T14:32:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/670b67f2-ec09-51e0-99c7-fd00bb42f632', 'word_count': 332, 'uri': 'nyt://article/670b67f2-ec09-51e0-99c7-fd00bb42f632'}, {'abstract': 'Both are pathbreaking women politicians who can’t get the respect they deserve.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/01/opinion/what-do-clinton-and-merkel-have-in-common.html', 'snippet': 'Both are pathbreaking women politicians who can’t get the respect they deserve.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — As a German, I guess it’s none of my business, but still — I’m excited about Hillary Clinton. As a woman, I feel she is in there for me, too. If things go right, for the first time in history, a woman, one of us, will rule the world. Go, Hillary! Get us that job!', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/opinion/sunday/01sauerbrey1-web/01sauerbrey1-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/29/opinion/sunday/01sauerbrey1-web/01sauerbrey1-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/opinion/sunday/01sauerbrey1-web/01sauerbrey1-web-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/opinion/sunday/01sauerbrey1-web/01sauerbrey1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 446, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/29/opinion/sunday/01sauerbrey1-web/01sauerbrey1-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 446}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/29/opinion/sunday/01sauerbrey1-web/01sauerbrey1-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 761, 'width': 1024,