ter the government dismissed 10,000 civil servants suspected of links to a failed coup in July.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Turkey Detains Prominent Opposition Journalists', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Turkey Detains Journalists as Crackdown Continues', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Yeginsu, Ceylan', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': "Coups D'Etat and Attempted Coups D'Etat", 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gulen, Fethullah', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cumhuriyet (Newspaper)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Human Rights and Human Rights Violations', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Detainees', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erdogan, Recep Tayyip', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of the Press', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T15:19:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Europe', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ceylan Yeginsu', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ceylan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yeginsu', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0438451e-8824-5055-8f99-232365e46ed5', 'word_count': 564, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0438451e-8824-5055-8f99-232365e46ed5'}, {'abstract': '“President Bartlet will call on you at a press conference after he discloses he has multiple sclerosis,” my sister Dottie said over the phone in 2001. Huh?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/01/insider/meet-the-leading-expert-on-political-leaders-health-and-his-west-wing-doppelganger.html', 'snippet': '“President Bartlet will call on you at a press conference after he discloses he has multiple sclerosis,” my sister Dottie said over the phone in 2001. Huh?', 'lead_paragraph': 'Times Insider shares historic insights from The New York Times. In this piece, Lawrence K. Altman, M.D. — a physician journalist whose Times interview with Ronald Reagan in 1980 about the then-presidential candidate’s health is believed to be the first of its kind — ruminates on his experience chronicling would-be leaders’ fitness for office from the ’70s to the present.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/insider/28-Insider-Altman-Image/28-Insider-Altman-Image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/10/27/insider/28-Insider-Altman-Image/28-Insider-Altman-Image-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/insider/28-Insider-Altman-Image/28-Insider-Altman-Image-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/insider/28-Insider-Altman-Image/28-Insider-Altman-Image-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/10/27/insider/28-Insider-Altman-Image/28-Insider-Altman-Image-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/10/27/insider/28-Insider-Altman-Image/28-Insider-