'', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Chigozie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Obioma', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}, {'firstname': 'Yiyun', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Li', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 4}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/077240a2-9e10-5269-8ea2-176ddef51695', 'word_count': 2906, 'uri': 'nyt://article/077240a2-9e10-5269-8ea2-176ddef51695'}, {'abstract': 'John Moeller, a veteran of three administrations, has created a Presidential Palate menu with the executive chef of Delmonico’s, Billy Oliva.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/02/dining/delmonicos-white-house-chef-john-moeller.html', 'snippet': 'John Moeller, a veteran of three administrations, has created a Presidential Palate menu with the executive chef of Delmonico’s, Billy Oliva.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Over the decades, Delmonico’s Restaurant has counted heads of state among its customers, including more than a dozen American presidents. Now the restaurant has turned to John Moeller, a former White House chef (from 1992 to 2005), to work with its executive chef, Billy Oliva, on a menu of dishes that have been served to commanders in chief at Delmonico’s and at the White House. The menu, including roast duck and sweet potato bisque, crab à la Newburg, turkey à la king, goulash and baked alaska, will be available from Tuesday to Nov. 8 for lunch and dinner: Presidential Palates menu, Delmonico’s Restaurant, 56 Beaver Street (South William Street), 212-509-1144, delmonicosrestaurant.com.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 900, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 900}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 683, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1366, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerdelmonicos/02burnerdelmonicos-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Delmonico’s Welcomes a White House Chef', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Commemorate: Delmonico’s Welcomes a White House Chef', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moeller, John', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Delmonico's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chefs', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T16:42:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/5892399e-4b27-5761-aad3-6738b8d5bf3b', 'word_count': 111, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5892399e-4b27-5761-aad3-6738b8d5bf3b'}, {'abstract': 'Across from Bryant Park, a playground for chocolate makers and lovers from the pastry chef Marc Aumont.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/02/dining/gabriel-kreuther-handcrafted-chocolate.html', 'snippet': 'Across from Bryant Park, a playground for chocolate makers and lovers from the pastry chef Marc Aumont.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The chocolate shop adjacent to Gabriel Kreuther’s restaurant has some compelling features. Chefs in a glass-encased space enrobe chocolates as visitors watch them work. The two display cases in the soaring shop tempt with chocolates and pastries, among them macarons with a series of fillings based on cheesecakes, a sort of France-meets-America concept, as the pastry chef, Marc Aumont, put it. Among the flavors, there is the inevitable pumpkin spice. A few cafe tables are set out in the metallic-flecked room for customers to enjoy coffee and sweets but not much else: Kreuther Handcrafted Chocolate, 43 West 42nd Street, 212-201-1985. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerchocolate1/02burnerchocolate1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/02/dining/02burnerchocolate1/02burnerchocolate1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank':