on’s many crimes is, in fact, Hillary Clinton. In 1974 she was, by many accounts, among the brightest members of the staff of the House Judiciary Committee that investigated Nixon and prepared the articles of impeachment. In this bizarre election year, it must be painful to her that she should find herself at the center of a scandal described by her hyperbolic political opponent, Donald J. Trump, as “worse than Watergate.”', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2016/11/01/opinion/31naftaliWeb/31naftaliWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Clinton’s Emails Matter', 'kicker': 'Op-Ed Contributor', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classified Information and State Secrets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Watergate Affair', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'E-Mail', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clinton, Hillary Rodham', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nixon, Richard Milhous', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Federal Bureau of Investigation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T19:37:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Timothy Naftali', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Timothy', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Naftali', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/70ab4828-c952-516e-9b19-fa0a740f4ddf', 'word_count': 811, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70ab4828-c952-516e-9b19-fa0a740f4ddf'}, {'abstract': 'JACK Quartet’s multimedia concoction, “Flight,” featured readings, video projections and music by the composer Roger Reynolds.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2016/11/01/arts/music/review-jack-quartet-flight-park-avenue-armory.html', 'snippet': 'JACK Quartet’s multimedia concoction, “Flight,” featured readings, video projections and music by the composer Roger Reynolds.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The armchairs in the Board of Officers Room at the Park Avenue Armory are surely the most comfortable concert-hall seats in New York. And yet I couldn’t stop squirming during Sunday afternoon’s performance there of “Flight,” a multimedia concoction for string quartet, electronics and video conceived by the composer Roger Reynolds. Billed as a tribute to humanity’s fascination with flying, the work draws on images and texts spanning some 3,000 years, and that’s about how long it felt, thanks to the flat-footed and dispiriting way in which it was all cobbled together.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Review: A Musical Homage to Aviation, From Plato to Earhart', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': ' Homage to Aviation, From Plato to Earhart', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'da Fonseca-Wollheim, Corinna', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'JACK Quartet', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Park Avenue Armory (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Flight (Musical Work)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Reynolds, Roger', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2016-10-31T19:51:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Corinna da Fonseca-Wollheim', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/f0753d71-7746-509b-bd97-3075dcd8efc8', 'word_count': 450, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f0753d71-7746-509b-bd97-3075dcd8efc8'}, {'abstract': 'Some lawmakers who favored an exit from the European Union had called for Mr. Carney to resign, saying he politicized the central bank.', 'web_url': 'https://